window.CLF_EXAMS=window.CLF_EXAMS||[];
window.CLF_EXAMS.push({"id":7,"qs":[{"id":"E2A-54","d":2,"ts":"2.1.7","t":"Iceberg time travel","q":"An auditor asks a data engineer to reproduce a quarterly revenue report exactly as it would have been calculated on 30 June 2026 at 23:59 UTC. The data is in an Apache Iceberg table named sales that has been updated many times since then, and snapshot retention is set to 1 year. The data engineer uses Amazon Athena. What is the MOST efficient way to produce the report?","o":["Restore the previous versions of the Parquet files with S3 Versioning and create a new table on them.","Rebuild the table from the raw source files and filter out records loaded after 30 June 2026.","Run the report query against sales with FOR TIMESTAMP AS OF TIMESTAMP '2026-06-30 23:59:00 UTC'.","Query the AWS CloudTrail logs to find which rows were changed after 30 June 2026 and reverse those changes."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'exactly as it would have been calculated on 30 June 2026', tabel 'Apache Iceberg', dan 'snapshot retention is set to 1 year'. Iceberg menyimpan snapshot setiap commit, sehingga Athena dapat menjalankan time travel query dengan klausa FOR TIMESTAMP AS OF (atau FOR VERSION AS OF untuk snapshot ID) untuk membaca tabel persis pada titik waktu tersebut, termasuk efek update dan delete. Karena retensi snapshot 1 tahun, snapshot akhir Juni masih tersedia. Distraktor terdekat adalah S3 Versioning: versi object tidak merepresentasikan state tabel yang konsisten (metadata, manifest, dan data file harus selaras), sehingga rekonstruksi rumit dan rawan salah. Membangun ulang dari data mentah tidak mencerminkan update/delete yang terjadi. CloudTrail tidak mencatat perubahan tingkat baris. Aturan umum: query state tabel di masa lalu pada Iceberg → time travel (FOR TIMESTAMP/VERSION AS OF), selama snapshot belum kedaluwarsa.","r":["Salah — Menyusun ulang tabel dari versi object S3 rumit dan tidak menjamin konsistensi metadata Iceberg.","Salah — Membangun ulang dari data mentah tidak merefleksikan update dan delete yang terjadi sebelum tanggal tersebut.","Benar — Time travel Iceberg di Athena membaca snapshot tabel pada timestamp yang diminta secara langsung.","Salah — CloudTrail mencatat panggilan API, bukan perubahan nilai baris di dalam tabel."],"k":"Report 'as of' a past time on Iceberg → Athena FOR TIMESTAMP AS OF (snapshot must still be retained)."},{"id":"E1A-54","d":1,"ts":"1.1.9","t":"DynamoDB on-demand capacity","q":"A startup ingests event data into an Amazon DynamoDB table. Traffic is highly unpredictable: it is near zero for hours and then spikes to thousands of writes per second during marketing campaigns. Writes are frequently throttled during spikes, and the team does not want to manage capacity planning. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Switch the table to on-demand capacity mode.","Increase provisioned write capacity to the peak value permanently.","Add a DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) cluster in front of the table.","Create a global secondary index on the table."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: trafik 'highly unpredictable', 'near zero' lalu 'spikes', dan 'does not want to manage capacity planning'. Mode kapasitas on-demand DynamoDB menyesuaikan kapasitas secara otomatis terhadap trafik dan ditagih per request, sehingga cocok untuk beban yang tidak dapat diprediksi dan menghilangkan perencanaan kapasitas. Distraktor terdekat adalah provisioned di nilai puncak: throttling hilang tetapi membayar kapasitas puncak sepanjang waktu walau trafik hampir nol. DAX adalah cache untuk baca, tidak membantu throttling tulis. GSI menambah beban tulis karena setiap tulis juga direplikasi ke index. Aturan umum: beban tidak terduga atau spiky = on-demand; beban stabil dan dapat diprediksi = provisioned + auto scaling (lebih murah).","r":["Benar — On-demand menyesuaikan kapasitas otomatis untuk lonjakan tanpa perencanaan kapasitas.","Salah — Membayar kapasitas puncak sepanjang waktu sangat boros untuk trafik yang sering mendekati nol.","Salah — DAX mempercepat baca, bukan mengatasi throttling tulis.","Salah — GSI menambah beban tulis, bukan mengurangi throttling."],"k":"DynamoDB trafik spiky/tidak terduga, tanpa capacity planning → on-demand mode."},{"id":"E2C-47","d":2,"ts":"2.4.6","t":"Choosing a vector store for Bedrock knowledge bases","q":"A company wants to build an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base over 80 million document chunks for an internal archive search tool. Queries are infrequent (a few hundred per day), sub-second latency is acceptable, and the company wants the MOST cost-effective vector storage without managing clusters. Which vector store should the data engineer choose?","o":["An Amazon S3 vector bucket (Amazon S3 Vectors) as the knowledge base vector store.","A provisioned Amazon OpenSearch Service domain with large memory-optimized data nodes.","An Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL cluster with pgvector sized for peak capacity at all times.","Amazon MemoryDB with vector search enabled."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah volume vektor besar, query 'infrequent', latensi sub-detik dapat diterima, dan 'MOST cost-effective ... without managing clusters'. Amazon S3 Vectors menyediakan vector bucket dengan penyimpanan dan query vektor yang tahan lama dan berbiaya rendah, serta didukung sebagai vector store untuk Amazon Bedrock knowledge base, sehingga cocok untuk dataset besar yang jarang di-query. OpenSearch domain provisioned memberikan latensi rendah dan fitur pencarian kaya, tetapi biaya node selalu berjalan dan harus dikelola. Aurora dengan pgvector yang disiapkan untuk kapasitas puncak juga mahal untuk beban kecil. MemoryDB menyimpan vektor di memori untuk latensi sangat rendah, yang paling mahal per GB dan berlebihan di sini. Perlu diingat, S3 Vectors membatasi custom metadata per vektor (1 KB dan 35 key untuk knowledge base), sehingga hierarchical chunking dengan jumlah token sangat besar dapat melampaui batas metadata tersebut. Aturan umum: banyak vektor + query jarang + biaya rendah → S3 Vectors; latensi sangat rendah → OpenSearch/MemoryDB.","r":["Benar — S3 Vectors menyimpan vektor dalam jumlah besar dengan biaya rendah tanpa cluster dan terintegrasi dengan knowledge base.","Salah — Domain OpenSearch provisioned mahal untuk beban query rendah dan perlu dikelola.","Salah — Cluster Aurora yang disiapkan untuk puncak membayar kapasitas yang jarang dipakai.","Salah — MemoryDB in-memory memberikan latensi sangat rendah yang tidak dibutuhkan dengan biaya per GB tertinggi."],"k":"Tips ujian: vektor sangat banyak, query jarang, paling murah → Amazon S3 Vectors."},{"id":"E1A-30","d":1,"ts":"1.1.5","t":"EventBridge Scheduler time zones","q":"An AWS Glue job must run every day at 01:00 in the Asia/Jakarta time zone, and a second job must run every day at 07:00 in the America/New_York time zone, which observes daylight saving time. The data engineer wants the schedules to follow local time automatically. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Create Amazon EventBridge Scheduler schedules with cron expressions and the appropriate time zone for each job, targeting the AWS Glue StartJobRun API.","Create AWS Glue scheduled triggers with cron expressions in UTC and update them manually twice a year.","Run a Lambda function every minute that checks the local time and starts the jobs.","Use an Amazon EC2 instance with crontab configured for each time zone."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: jadwal harus mengikuti 'local time' dan salah satunya mengikuti 'daylight saving time', dengan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Amazon EventBridge Scheduler mendukung cron expression dengan zona waktu IANA (misalnya America/New_York) dan otomatis menyesuaikan DST; targetnya bisa langsung API Glue StartJobRun melalui universal target. Distraktor terdekat adalah Glue scheduled trigger: cron Glue (dan aturan terjadwal EventBridge klasik) dievaluasi dalam UTC sehingga harus diubah manual saat DST berganti. Lambda yang berjalan tiap menit membuang biaya dan menambah kode. Crontab di EC2 berarti mengelola server. Aturan umum: jadwal dengan zona waktu/DST, one-time schedule, atau jadwal dalam jumlah besar = EventBridge Scheduler.","r":["Benar — EventBridge Scheduler mendukung zona waktu dan DST serta bisa langsung memanggil Glue StartJobRun.","Salah — Cron Glue berbasis UTC, sehingga perlu penyesuaian manual saat DST berubah.","Salah — Polling tiap menit dengan Lambda menambah biaya dan kode yang tidak perlu.","Salah — Crontab di EC2 menambah pengelolaan server."],"k":"Jadwal dengan time zone / DST → EventBridge Scheduler (bukan cron UTC)."},{"id":"E1B-08","d":1,"ts":"1.2.5","t":"Glue Python shell vs Lambda vs Glue Spark","q":"A data engineer must build a daily job that calls a partner REST API, retrieves about 200 MB of JSON data, applies simple pandas transformations, and writes the result to Amazon S3. Because of API pagination limits, the job takes about 40 minutes to complete. The company wants the MOST cost-effective serverless solution. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create an AWS Lambda function with 10 GB of memory and schedule it with Amazon EventBridge.","Create an AWS Glue Spark ETL job with 10 G.2X workers.","Launch a transient Amazon EMR cluster each day to run the Python script as a step.","Create an AWS Glue Python shell job and schedule it with a Glue trigger."],"a":[3],"e":"Faktor penentunya adalah durasi sekitar '40 minutes', ukuran data kecil (200 MB), transformasi pandas sederhana, dan 'MOST cost-effective serverless'. AWS Glue Python shell job menjalankan skrip Python biasa (termasuk pandas) dengan kapasitas kecil (0.0625 atau 1 DPU), tanpa batas 15 menit, sehingga sangat murah untuk tugas ringan yang berjalan lama. Lambda adalah distraktor terdekat, tetapi batas timeout 15 menit membuat job 40 menit gagal. Glue Spark job dengan 10 worker G.2X jauh terlalu besar dan mahal untuk 200 MB. EMR transient cluster menambah biaya EC2 dan overhead pengelolaan. Aturan umum: skrip Python ringan yang lebih dari 15 menit → Glue Python shell; data besar terdistribusi → Glue Spark.","r":["Salah — Lambda dibatasi 15 menit, sehingga job 40 menit akan timeout.","Salah — Spark dengan 10 worker G.2X berlebihan untuk 200 MB dan biayanya jauh lebih tinggi.","Salah — EMR bukan serverless dan menambah biaya serta overhead cluster untuk skrip kecil.","Benar — Python shell job murah (pecahan DPU), mendukung pandas, dan tidak terkena batas 15 menit."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'small data + Python/pandas + runs longer than 15 minutes' → AWS Glue Python shell job."},{"id":"E2A-09","d":2,"ts":"2.1.1","t":"Kinesis Data Streams capacity modes","q":"A logistics company ingests telemetry from delivery vehicles into a stream that custom consumer applications process in real time. Throughput varies from 1 MB/s at night to 40 MB/s during peak hours, and new vehicle fleets are added without notice. The team does not want to monitor shard utilization or perform resharding. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Amazon Kinesis Data Streams in provisioned mode with an AWS Lambda function that splits shards when utilization exceeds 80%","Amazon Kinesis Data Streams in on-demand mode","Amazon MSK provisioned cluster sized for the 40 MB/s peak","Amazon Data Firehose with a 1 MB buffer size delivering to the consumer applications"],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci adalah throughput yang bervariasi dan tidak terduga, 'custom consumer applications process in real time', serta tidak ingin 'monitor shard utilization or perform resharding'. Kinesis Data Streams on-demand mode otomatis menyesuaikan kapasitas sesuai trafik tanpa perlu mengelola jumlah shard, sambil tetap mendukung consumer kustom real time. Distraktor terdekat adalah provisioned mode dengan Lambda untuk split shard: bisa bekerja, tetapi justru membangun otomatisasi yang ingin dihindari. MSK provisioned berukuran untuk puncak membayar kapasitas idle dan tetap perlu mengelola broker. Firehose adalah layanan delivery ke tujuan tertentu (S3, Redshift, OpenSearch, dan lain-lain), bukan stream yang dibaca consumer kustom. Aturan umum: trafik stream tak terduga dan tidak mau kelola shard → Kinesis Data Streams on-demand.","r":["Salah — Mengotomasi resharding sendiri menambah kode dan monitoring, bertentangan dengan syarat overhead minimal.","Benar — On-demand mode menskalakan kapasitas otomatis tanpa manajemen shard dan tetap mendukung consumer kustom.","Salah — Cluster yang diukur untuk puncak membayar kapasitas idle sepanjang malam dan masih memerlukan pengelolaan broker.","Salah — Firehose tidak menyediakan stream yang dibaca consumer kustom secara real time; ia mengirim data ke destinasi yang didukung."],"k":"Variable/unknown stream throughput + no shard management → Kinesis Data Streams on-demand."},{"id":"E4B-55","d":4,"ts":"4.5.6","t":"SageMaker Catalog subscription workflow","q":"A company uses Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio. The Sales project has published a curated orders table as an asset in Amazon SageMaker Catalog. A data analyst in the Marketing project finds the asset and needs to query it with Amazon Athena from the Marketing project. Data owners must approve every access request, and the company wants no manual permission management. What should the analyst do?","o":["Ask the AWS account administrator to attach an IAM policy that grants direct S3 access to the orders data.","Ask a data engineer to copy the orders table into the Marketing project's S3 location.","Ask the Lake Formation administrator to grant SELECT on the orders table to the analyst's IAM user.","Submit a subscription request for the asset from the Marketing project with a business justification; after a member of the Sales project approves it, SageMaker Catalog automatically grants the Marketing project access to the table."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: akses dari 'the Marketing project', 'data owners must approve every access request', dan 'no manual permission management'. Di SageMaker Catalog, consumer mengajukan subscription request dari proyeknya; anggota proyek pemilik (Sales) meninjau lalu menyetujui atau menolak. Untuk managed asset seperti tabel AWS Glue, setelah disetujui SageMaker Catalog secara otomatis membuat grant (misalnya izin Lake Formation) ke role proyek consumer, sehingga semua anggota proyek Marketing dapat meng-query dengan Athena. Distraktor terdekat adalah grant Lake Formation manual oleh admin: berhasil secara teknis, tetapi melewati alur approval pemilik data dan menambah pekerjaan manual. IAM policy langsung ke S3 melewati governance Lake Formation dan katalog. Menyalin tabel menciptakan duplikasi dan data basi. Aturan umum: akses data di SageMaker Catalog → subscription request dari project → approval owner → grant otomatis ke project.","r":["Salah — Akses S3 langsung melewati governance katalog dan approval pemilik data.","Salah — Menyalin tabel menciptakan duplikasi dan melewati kontrol akses terkelola.","Salah — Grant manual menambah overhead dan melewati alur approval pemilik data.","Benar — Subscription request dari project dengan approval pemilik menghasilkan grant otomatis ke project."],"k":"Tips ujian: SageMaker Catalog access → subscribe from project → owner approves → automatic grant to project."},{"id":"E2C-19","d":2,"ts":"2.4.2","t":"DMS DDL change handling during CDC","q":"A company uses an AWS DMS task with full load and change data capture (CDC) to replicate an Amazon RDS for MySQL database to Amazon Aurora MySQL. The application team regularly adds columns to source tables during releases. The data engineer wants these column additions to be applied to the target automatically while the task keeps running. What should the data engineer configure?","o":["Stop the DMS task before each release, alter the target tables manually, and restart the task with a new full load.","Enable the DMS task's change processing DDL handling setting so that ALTER TABLE changes on the source are applied to the target.","Use AWS DMS Schema Conversion to convert the schema again after each release.","Replace DMS with a daily mysqldump export and import."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah perubahan DDL (penambahan kolom) di sumber yang harus 'applied to the target automatically while the task keeps running'. AWS DMS memiliki task settings untuk penanganan DDL pada CDC, yaitu ChangeProcessingDdlHandlingPolicy dengan opsi seperti HandleSourceTableAltered, yang menerapkan ALTER TABLE dari sumber ke target untuk endpoint yang mendukungnya. Dengan begitu replikasi tetap berjalan dan schema target mengikuti perubahan. Menghentikan task dan melakukan full load ulang setiap rilis menambah downtime dan overhead. DMS Schema Conversion dipakai untuk migrasi heterogen dan konversi awal schema/kode, bukan untuk sinkronisasi DDL berkelanjutan pada migrasi homogen. mysqldump harian kehilangan sifat near real time CDC. Aturan umum: perubahan schema saat CDC DMS → aktifkan DDL handling (HandleSourceTableAltered).","r":["Salah — Menghentikan task dan full load ulang setiap rilis menimbulkan downtime dan pekerjaan manual.","Benar — Pengaturan DDL handling di DMS menerapkan ALTER TABLE dari sumber ke target selama CDC berjalan.","Salah — DMS Schema Conversion untuk konversi heterogen awal, bukan untuk mengikuti perubahan DDL saat replikasi berjalan.","Salah — Dump harian menghilangkan replikasi berkelanjutan dan menambah latensi."],"k":"Tips ujian: DMS CDC + kolom baru di sumber → ChangeProcessingDdlHandlingPolicy (HandleSourceTableAltered)."},{"id":"E4A-09","d":4,"ts":"4.1.3","t":"Secrets Manager automatic rotation","q":"An application stores the credentials for an Amazon Aurora MySQL database as plaintext in a configuration file on Amazon EC2. A new compliance rule requires that the database password be rotated automatically every 30 days and that applications always retrieve the current password at runtime. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Store the credentials in AWS Secrets Manager, turn on automatic rotation with a 30-day schedule, and update the application to retrieve the secret by using the AWS SDK.","Store the credentials as an AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store SecureString parameter, and create an Amazon EventBridge schedule that invokes a custom Lambda function to change the password every 30 days.","Enable automatic key rotation on the AWS KMS key that encrypts the Aurora cluster.","Create an IAM user for the application and rotate the user's access keys every 30 days by using a scheduled script."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'rotated automatically every 30 days' dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. AWS Secrets Manager punya fitur rotasi bawaan untuk Amazon RDS, Aurora, dan Redshift dengan fungsi rotasi yang disediakan AWS, sehingga Anda hanya menentukan jadwal. Aplikasi lalu mengambil secret saat runtime dengan SDK dan selalu mendapat versi AWSCURRENT. Parameter Store SecureString bisa menyimpan password, tetapi tidak punya rotasi bawaan sehingga Anda harus membangun dan memelihara logika rotasi sendiri. Rotasi KMS key hanya mengganti material kunci enkripsi, bukan password database. Access key IAM user tidak berhubungan dengan password database Aurora. Aturan umum: 'rotate database credentials automatically' → Secrets Manager.","r":["Benar — Secrets Manager menyediakan rotasi otomatis terjadwal untuk Aurora dan pengambilan secret saat runtime dengan overhead minimal.","Salah — Bisa berfungsi, tetapi Parameter Store tidak punya rotasi bawaan sehingga logika rotasi custom menambah overhead.","Salah — Rotasi KMS key mengganti kunci enkripsi data, bukan password user database.","Salah — Access key IAM tidak dipakai untuk login dengan password ke Aurora MySQL."],"k":"Tips ujian: rotasi otomatis password database → Secrets Manager; Parameter Store tidak punya rotasi bawaan."},{"id":"E4A-21","d":4,"ts":"4.1.5","t":"Redshift-managed VPC endpoints","q":"A BI team in a separate AWS account runs reporting tools in its own VPC. The tools need private SQL connectivity to an Amazon Redshift RA3 provisioned cluster in the data platform account. The cluster must stay not publicly accessible, and the data platform team does not want to manage VPC peering or route tables between the accounts. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create a Redshift-managed VPC endpoint for the cluster in the BI team's VPC after granting the BI account access to the cluster.","Create an interface VPC endpoint for the com.amazonaws.region.redshift service in the BI team's VPC.","Turn on the publicly accessible setting and restrict the cluster security group to the BI team's NAT gateway IP addresses.","Create an S3 gateway endpoint in the BI team's VPC and enable enhanced VPC routing on the cluster."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'private SQL connectivity', 'separate AWS account', dan 'not ... manage VPC peering or route tables'. Redshift-managed VPC endpoint (berbasis AWS PrivateLink) memungkinkan cluster RA3 atau Redshift Serverless diakses secara privat dari VPC lain, termasuk akun lain, setelah pemilik cluster memberi izin akses ke akun tersebut. Endpoint muncul sebagai alamat privat di VPC BI tanpa peering atau perubahan routing. Interface endpoint untuk service com.amazonaws.region.redshift hanya untuk memanggil Redshift API manajemen (misalnya DescribeClusters), bukan koneksi SQL ke port cluster. Membuat cluster publik melanggar syarat. Enhanced VPC routing mengatur traffic COPY/UNLOAD ke S3, bukan koneksi klien. Aturan umum: koneksi SQL privat lintas VPC/akun ke Redshift → Redshift-managed VPC endpoint.","r":["Benar — Redshift-managed VPC endpoint memberi akses SQL privat lintas akun ke cluster RA3 tanpa peering.","Salah — Endpoint ini hanya untuk Redshift API manajemen, bukan koneksi JDBC/ODBC ke database.","Salah — Melanggar syarat cluster tidak boleh publicly accessible.","Salah — Enhanced VPC routing dan S3 endpoint hanya memengaruhi traffic data ke S3, bukan koneksi BI ke cluster."],"k":"Tips ujian: interface endpoint 'redshift' = API manajemen; akses SQL lintas VPC/akun = Redshift-managed VPC endpoint."},{"id":"E2B-42","d":2,"ts":"2.3.3","t":"Abort incomplete multipart uploads","q":"A data ingestion application uploads large files to Amazon S3 by using multipart upload. Network interruptions sometimes cause uploads to fail midway. The S3 bill shows storage that does not correspond to any visible objects in the bucket. Which solution will remove this storage automatically?","o":["Enable S3 Transfer Acceleration on the bucket.","Add an S3 Lifecycle rule with an Expiration action of 1 day for all objects.","Enable S3 Versioning and delete noncurrent versions after 1 day.","Add an S3 Lifecycle rule with an AbortIncompleteMultipartUpload action that runs 7 days after an upload is initiated."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'multipart upload', 'fail midway' dan storage yang 'does not correspond to any visible objects'. Part dari multipart upload yang tidak selesai tetap tersimpan dan ditagih, tetapi tidak terlihat sebagai objek. Lifecycle action AbortIncompleteMultipartUpload membatalkan upload yang belum selesai setelah sejumlah hari sejak dimulai dan menghapus part-nya. Expiration 1 hari akan menghapus objek valid dan tidak berlaku untuk part yang belum selesai. Versioning tidak berhubungan dengan multipart upload yang tidak lengkap. Transfer Acceleration mempercepat upload, tetapi tidak membersihkan part yang tertinggal. Ingat: biaya 'tak terlihat' dari upload gagal → AbortIncompleteMultipartUpload.","r":["Salah — Transfer Acceleration hanya mempercepat transfer, tidak membersihkan part yang tertinggal.","Salah — Expiration menghapus objek yang valid dan tidak menangani part upload yang belum selesai.","Salah — Versioning tidak berhubungan dengan multipart upload yang tidak lengkap.","Benar — AbortIncompleteMultipartUpload menghapus part dari upload yang gagal secara otomatis."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'storage tidak terlihat' / failed multipart uploads → Lifecycle AbortIncompleteMultipartUpload."},{"id":"E3A-21","d":3,"ts":"3.1.6","t":"AWS Glue DataBrew recipes","q":"Business analysts receive weekly CSV files in Amazon S3 that contain inconsistent date formats, duplicate rows, extra whitespace, and a full-name column that must be split into first and last name. The analysts do not write code. They want to build the cleanup steps visually once and then run the same steps automatically every week. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Write an AWS Glue PySpark script with the required transformations and schedule it with a Glue trigger.","Create an AWS Glue DataBrew project to build a recipe interactively, then create a scheduled DataBrew recipe job that applies the recipe to each new file.","Load the files into Amazon Redshift and ask the analysts to write SQL cleanup scripts.","Use Amazon Athena CREATE VIEW statements to clean the data at query time."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'analysts do not write code', 'build visually once', dan 'run the same steps automatically every week'. AWS Glue DataBrew adalah alat persiapan data visual dengan lebih dari 250 transformasi siap pakai, misalnya format tanggal, hapus duplikat, trim spasi, dan split kolom. Langkah-langkah yang dibuat di project disimpan sebagai recipe, lalu recipe dijalankan pada seluruh data oleh recipe job yang bisa dijadwalkan. Script Glue PySpark membutuhkan coding. Redshift SQL dan view Athena juga membutuhkan penulisan SQL dan tidak visual. Aturan umum: persiapan data no-code yang bisa diulang → DataBrew project + recipe + scheduled job.","r":["Salah — Membutuhkan penulisan kode PySpark, padahal analis tidak menulis kode.","Benar — DataBrew menyediakan transformasi visual yang disimpan sebagai recipe dan dijalankan oleh job terjadwal.","Salah — Membutuhkan skill SQL dan memuat data ke warehouse hanya untuk cleanup.","Salah — View Athena butuh SQL dan membersihkan data setiap kali query, bukan menghasilkan data bersih."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'no-code / visual data preparation, reusable steps' → Glue DataBrew recipe + job."},{"id":"E3A-66","d":3,"ts":"3.2.6","t":"Pivoting with conditional aggregation","q":"An analyst has a query result in Amazon Athena with rows of (region, month, revenue), where month is a value from 'Jan' to 'Dec'. A report requires one row per region with twelve columns, one for each month's revenue. Which approach produces this pivoted result in Athena?","o":["Use the PIVOT clause: SELECT * FROM sales PIVOT (SUM(revenue) FOR month IN ('Jan', 'Feb', ...)).","Use conditional aggregation: SELECT region, SUM(CASE WHEN month = 'Jan' THEN revenue END) AS jan, SUM(CASE WHEN month = 'Feb' THEN revenue END) AS feb, ... FROM sales GROUP BY region.","Use GROUP BY region, month ORDER BY month.","Use UNION ALL to stack the twelve monthly result sets into one column."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'one row per region with twelve columns' yang merupakan definisi pivoting, yaitu mengubah nilai baris (bulan) menjadi kolom, dan engine 'Athena'. Athena (berbasis Trino) tidak mendukung klausa PIVOT, sehingga pola standarnya adalah conditional aggregation: SUM(CASE WHEN month = 'Jan' THEN revenue END) untuk setiap bulan, lalu GROUP BY region. Klausa PIVOT memang didukung di Amazon Redshift, tetapi tidak di Athena, jadi itu jebakan. GROUP BY region, month tetap menghasilkan satu baris per kombinasi region dan bulan, yaitu format panjang. UNION ALL menumpuk baris, yang merupakan kebalikan dari pivot (lebih mirip unpivot). Aturan umum: pivot = baris menjadi kolom; di SQL yang tidak punya PIVOT, gunakan agregasi dengan CASE WHEN; di Quick Sight bisa juga memakai visual pivot table.","r":["Salah — Athena (Trino) tidak mendukung klausa PIVOT; klausa itu didukung di Redshift.","Benar — Conditional aggregation dengan CASE WHEN per bulan dan GROUP BY region menghasilkan bentuk pivot.","Salah — Masih menghasilkan satu baris per region per bulan (format panjang).","Salah — UNION ALL menumpuk baris, kebalikan dari pivot."],"k":"Tips ujian: pivot di Athena → SUM(CASE WHEN ... THEN ... END) + GROUP BY; Redshift punya PIVOT/UNPIVOT."},{"id":"E1B-54","d":1,"ts":"1.2.7","t":"Athena missing partitions","q":"A daily AWS Glue job writes Parquet output to Amazon S3 in new Hive-style partition folders such as dt=2026-10-14/. The table is defined in the AWS Glue Data Catalog. Analysts report that Amazon Athena queries return no rows for the newest dates, although the files exist in S3. Which solution will resolve the issue with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Recreate the Athena table every morning with a CREATE EXTERNAL TABLE statement.","Configure the Glue job's S3 sink with enableUpdateCatalog and partitionKeys so that new partitions are registered in the Data Catalog during each run.","Increase the Athena query timeout for the workgroup.","Convert the output to CSV so that Athena can discover new files automatically."],"a":[1],"e":"Gejala kuncinya adalah file untuk tanggal baru 'exist in S3' tetapi Athena 'return no rows for the newest dates', yang berarti partisi baru belum terdaftar di Data Catalog. Athena hanya memindai partisi yang dikenal katalog (kecuali memakai partition projection). Mengonfigurasi sink Glue dengan enableUpdateCatalog dan partitionKeys membuat job mendaftarkan partisi baru setiap kali menulis, tanpa langkah tambahan. Membuat ulang tabel setiap pagi tidak menambahkan partisi kecuali diikuti MSCK REPAIR TABLE dan menambah pekerjaan manual. Menaikkan timeout tidak relevan karena query berhasil tetapi tidak menemukan partisi. CSV tidak membuat partisi terdeteksi otomatis. Aturan umum: data baru tidak muncul di Athena → partisi belum terdaftar → update catalog dari job, MSCK REPAIR/ALTER TABLE ADD PARTITION, crawler, atau partition projection.","r":["Salah — Membuat ulang tabel tidak mendaftarkan partisi dan menambah pekerjaan manual.","Benar — Job mendaftarkan partisi baru ke Data Catalog secara otomatis di setiap run.","Salah — Query tidak timeout; partisinya saja yang tidak terdaftar.","Salah — Format file tidak memengaruhi pendaftaran partisi di katalog."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'files in S3 but Athena returns nothing for new partitions' → register partitions (enableUpdateCatalog, MSCK REPAIR, crawler, partition projection)."},{"id":"E1A-52","d":1,"ts":"1.1.8","t":"AWS DMS network allowlisting","q":"A company is migrating an on-premises Microsoft SQL Server database to Amazon S3 with AWS DMS. The on-premises network is connected to the VPC through AWS Site-to-Site VPN, and the corporate firewall blocks all inbound database connections except from allowlisted IP addresses. The database must not be exposed to the internet. Which TWO actions should a data engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Make the replication instance publicly accessible and allowlist the AWS DMS public IP ranges for the Region.","Create the DMS replication instance in a private subnet of the VPC that has a route to the on-premises network through the VPN.","Open the SQL Server port on the on-premises firewall to 0.0.0.0/0 during the migration.","Add the replication instance's private IP address (or the subnet CIDR) to the on-premises firewall allowlist for the SQL Server port.","Add an S3 bucket policy that allows the on-premises firewall's IP address."],"a":[1,3],"e":"Kata kunci: koneksi melalui 'Site-to-Site VPN', firewall memakai 'allowlisted IP addresses', dan database 'must not be exposed to the internet'. Replication instance DMS di subnet privat yang memiliki rute ke jaringan on-premises lewat VPN akan menghubungi SQL Server memakai IP privat. Firewall on-premises cukup meng-allowlist IP privat replication instance (atau CIDR subnet-nya) pada port SQL Server, sehingga database tidak terekspos ke internet. Distraktor terdekat adalah replication instance publik dengan allowlist IP publik DMS: lalu lintas berjalan di internet dan rentang IP terlalu luas. Membuka 0.0.0.0/0 jelas melanggar persyaratan. Bucket policy S3 tidak berhubungan dengan konektivitas ke database sumber. Aturan umum: DMS ke database on-prem = konektivitas privat (VPN/Direct Connect) + allowlist IP replication instance.","r":["Salah — Koneksi publik mengekspos database ke internet dan rentang IP terlalu luas.","Benar — Replication instance di subnet privat dengan rute VPN menjaga koneksi tetap privat.","Salah — Membuka port ke 0.0.0.0/0 mengekspos database ke seluruh internet.","Benar — Firewall on-premises perlu meng-allowlist IP privat replication instance agar koneksi masuk diizinkan.","Salah — Bucket policy S3 tidak memengaruhi koneksi DMS ke database sumber."],"k":"DMS ke DB on-prem privat → replication instance di subnet privat via VPN/DX + allowlist IP-nya di firewall."},{"id":"E1B-31","d":1,"ts":"1.2.4","t":"AWS Glue Flex execution class","q":"A company runs about 40 AWS Glue Spark ETL jobs each night that prepare data for reports used the next afternoon. The jobs have no strict start or completion time as long as they finish within several hours. The company wants to reduce the cost of these jobs without rewriting code. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Run the jobs with the AWS Glue Flex execution class.","Convert the jobs to AWS Glue Python shell jobs.","Change the jobs to use the G.4X worker type.","Migrate the jobs to a long-running Amazon EMR cluster with On-Demand Instances."],"a":[0],"e":"Penentunya adalah job yang 'no strict start or completion time' (tidak mendesak) dan keinginan 'reduce the cost' tanpa menulis ulang kode. Flex execution class di AWS Glue menjalankan job Spark di kapasitas cadangan dengan harga per DPU-hour yang lebih rendah daripada kelas standar, sehingga cocok untuk job yang toleran terhadap waktu mulai dan durasi yang bervariasi. Python shell job adalah distraktor yang lebih murah per DPU, tetapi tidak menjalankan Spark sehingga kode harus ditulis ulang dan tidak cocok untuk data besar. Worker G.4X lebih besar dan lebih mahal. Cluster EMR On-Demand yang berjalan terus menambah biaya dan pengelolaan. Aturan umum: Glue job non-urgent (dev/test, batch fleksibel) → Flex execution class.","r":["Benar — Flex menurunkan biaya untuk job Spark non-urgent tanpa perubahan kode.","Salah — Python shell bukan Spark; kode harus ditulis ulang dan tidak cocok untuk volume besar.","Salah — G.4X adalah worker yang lebih besar dan lebih mahal per jam.","Salah — Cluster On-Demand yang berjalan terus lebih mahal dan menambah overhead."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'Glue job + not time-sensitive + lower cost' → Flex execution class."},{"id":"E2B-19","d":2,"ts":"2.2.4","t":"Partition projection limitations","q":"A data engineer enabled Athena partition projection on a Data Catalog table to avoid running crawlers. The same table is also read by Apache Spark jobs on Amazon EMR that use the Glue Data Catalog as the metastore. Athena queries work, but the Spark jobs return no rows for any date after projection was enabled. New data is written to the table by an AWS Glue ETL job. Which solution will make the new partitions available to both Athena and Spark with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Configure the Glue ETL job to write with partitionKeys and enableUpdateCatalog set to true so that each run registers its new partitions in the Data Catalog.","Add the partition projection properties to the EMR spark-defaults configuration classification.","Create a partition index on the table's date column in the Data Catalog.","Configure Athena query result reuse so that Spark can read the Athena results."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: partition projection hanya berlaku untuk Athena, sedangkan 'Spark jobs on Amazon EMR' membaca partisi dari Data Catalog. Karena partisi baru tidak lagi didaftarkan, Spark tidak melihatnya. Cara paling ringan adalah membuat Glue ETL job yang menulis data juga mendaftarkan partisinya: dengan enableUpdateCatalog=true dan partitionKeys, sink Glue menambahkan partisi baru ke Data Catalog saat menulis, tanpa crawler. Athena tetap memakai projection, dan Spark membaca partisi yang terdaftar. Spark tidak memahami properti projection Athena, jadi menambahkannya ke spark-defaults tidak berpengaruh. Partition index hanya mempercepat lookup partisi yang sudah terdaftar. Query result reuse adalah cache di Athena. Ingat: partition projection = Athena-only; engine lain butuh partisi yang benar-benar terdaftar di catalog.","r":["Benar — Sink Glue dengan enableUpdateCatalog mendaftarkan partisi baru di catalog saat menulis, sehingga Spark juga melihatnya.","Salah — Partition projection adalah fitur Athena; Spark mengabaikan properti tersebut.","Salah — Partition index mempercepat pencarian partisi yang sudah terdaftar, bukan mendaftarkan partisi baru.","Salah — Result reuse adalah cache hasil Athena dan tidak memengaruhi metadata yang dibaca Spark."],"k":"Tips ujian: partition projection hanya untuk Athena; untuk EMR/Spectrum/Glue partisi harus terdaftar (crawler, MSCK, API, enableUpdateCatalog)."},{"id":"E1C-47","d":1,"ts":"1.4.1","t":"Spark code optimization","q":"A PySpark job on AWS Glue transforms 2 TB of data. Profiling shows two bottlenecks: a Python UDF that applies upper(), trim(), and a date parse to every row, and a step that calls collect() on the full DataFrame to build a list before writing each element to Amazon S3. Which combination of changes will reduce runtime the MOST? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Replace the Python UDF with built-in Spark SQL functions such as upper, trim, and to_date.","Increase only the driver memory so collect() does not run out of memory.","Remove collect() and write the DataFrame directly with the distributed DataFrame writer to Amazon S3.","Call repartition(1) before writing so that a single output file is produced.","Convert the Spark DataFrame to a pandas DataFrame for the transformation."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Dua bottleneck: 'Python UDF ... to every row' dan 'collect() on the full DataFrame'. Fungsi bawaan Spark SQL dieksekusi di JVM dan dioptimalkan oleh Catalyst, sedangkan Python UDF memaksa serialisasi data per baris antara JVM dan Python sehingga sangat lambat. collect() menarik seluruh 2 TB data ke satu driver, menghilangkan paralelisme; DataFrame writer menulis langsung dari para executor secara terdistribusi. Distractor terdekat adalah menambah memori driver: mungkin mencegah error memori, tetapi semua data tetap diproses di satu node. repartition(1) dan konversi ke pandas juga memusatkan pekerjaan di satu proses. Aturan umum: di Spark, utamakan fungsi bawaan daripada UDF dan hindari collect()/toPandas() pada data besar.","r":["Benar — Fungsi bawaan berjalan di JVM dengan optimasi Catalyst, jauh lebih cepat daripada Python UDF.","Salah — Data tetap terkumpul di driver sehingga pemrosesan tidak paralel.","Benar — Writer terdistribusi menulis dari semua executor secara paralel.","Salah — Satu partisi membuat penulisan berjalan di satu task saja.","Salah — pandas berjalan di satu node dan tidak muat untuk 2 TB."],"k":"Tips ujian: Spark lambat → ganti Python UDF dengan built-in functions, hindari collect()/toPandas()."},{"id":"E3A-04","d":3,"ts":"3.1.1","t":"Step Functions .sync and Retry","q":"An AWS Step Functions workflow starts an AWS Glue job and then loads the output into Amazon Redshift. Currently the workflow uses a Wait state of 20 minutes after starting the Glue job, but the job duration varies from 5 to 50 minutes, and the Glue job sometimes fails because of transient network errors. Which TWO changes should a data engineer make to make the workflow reliable? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Use the Glue StartJobRun service integration with the .sync (Run a Job) pattern so the state waits until the job finishes.","Convert the workflow to an Express workflow to reduce cost and latency.","Add a Retry field on the Glue task state with IntervalSeconds, BackoffRate, and MaxAttempts.","Increase the Wait state to 60 minutes so that the longest job always finishes.","Add a Parallel state that starts the Glue job twice and uses the first result."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Ada dua masalah: durasi job yang bervariasi ('5 to 50 minutes') dan 'transient network errors'. Untuk masalah pertama, pola integrasi .sync membuat Step Functions menunggu Glue job benar-benar selesai lalu melanjutkan dengan status sukses/gagal yang sebenarnya, tanpa menebak waktu. Untuk masalah kedua, field Retry dengan IntervalSeconds, BackoffRate (exponential backoff), dan MaxAttempts otomatis mengulang task saat error sementara. Wait 60 menit hanya membuang waktu dan tetap tidak tahu apakah job gagal. Express workflow tidak mendukung pola .sync maupun callback, dan durasinya maksimal 5 menit, jadi justru tidak cocok. Menjalankan job dua kali secara paralel boros dan bisa menimbulkan data duplikat. Aturan umum: tunggu job dengan .sync, tangani error sementara dengan Retry + backoff, tangani error permanen dengan Catch.","r":["Benar — .sync menunggu Glue job selesai berapa pun durasinya dan meneruskan status sebenarnya.","Salah — Express workflow tidak mendukung pola .sync dan dibatasi maksimal 5 menit, sedangkan job bisa 50 menit.","Benar — Retry dengan exponential backoff mengatasi kegagalan sementara secara otomatis.","Salah — Wait tetap tebakan waktu, memperlambat pipeline, dan tidak mendeteksi job yang gagal.","Salah — Menjalankan job ganda boros biaya dan berisiko menulis data duplikat."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'durasi job bervariasi' → .sync; 'transient error' → Retry + BackoffRate; Express workflow tidak mendukung .sync."},{"id":"E2A-42","d":2,"ts":"2.1.5","t":"Redshift streaming ingestion","q":"A company streams payment events into Amazon Kinesis Data Streams. Analysts need the events available in Amazon Redshift within seconds for fraud dashboards. The company wants the LOWEST latency and does not want to stage the data in Amazon S3 or manage any additional ingestion service. What should a data engineer do?","o":["Configure Amazon Data Firehose to read from the stream and deliver to Amazon Redshift using COPY from an intermediate S3 bucket.","Write an AWS Lambda function that reads from the stream and runs INSERT statements for each record.","Use AWS Glue streaming ETL jobs to write micro-batches to Amazon S3 and run COPY every minute.","Use Amazon Redshift streaming ingestion by creating an external schema for the Kinesis stream and a materialized view that consumes it."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'within seconds', 'LOWEST latency', serta 'does not want to stage the data in Amazon S3 or manage any additional ingestion service'. Redshift streaming ingestion membaca langsung dari Kinesis Data Streams atau Amazon MSK melalui external schema, lalu data masuk ke materialized view yang di-refresh (bisa otomatis) dengan latensi rendah, tanpa staging di S3. Distraktor terdekat adalah Data Firehose ke Redshift: pilihan managed yang populer, tetapi Firehose melakukan buffering dan staging ke S3 sebelum COPY, sehingga latensinya lebih tinggi dan melanggar syarat tanpa staging. Lambda dengan INSERT per record tidak efisien untuk Redshift dan menambah kode. Glue streaming + COPY menambah layanan dan staging. Aturan umum: Kinesis/MSK ke Redshift dengan latensi terendah tanpa S3 → Redshift streaming ingestion (materialized view).","r":["Salah — Firehose mem-buffer dan men-stage data di S3 sebelum COPY, sehingga latensi lebih tinggi dan melanggar syarat.","Salah — INSERT per baris sangat tidak efisien di Redshift dan memerlukan kode kustom.","Salah — Glue streaming menambah layanan dan staging S3 yang ingin dihindari.","Benar — Streaming ingestion mengonsumsi stream langsung ke materialized view dengan latensi rendah tanpa staging S3."],"k":"Kinesis/MSK → Redshift, lowest latency, no S3 staging → Redshift streaming ingestion (materialized view)."},{"id":"E4A-03","d":4,"ts":"4.1.1","t":"Stateful security group rules for DMS","q":"A company uses AWS DMS to migrate an on-premises Oracle database (port 1521) to Amazon Aurora MySQL (port 3306) over AWS Direct Connect. The DMS replication instance and the Aurora cluster each have their own security group. The security team has removed the default 'allow all' outbound rule from every security group in the VPC. Which THREE security group rules are required for the migration to work? (Choose THREE.)","o":["An outbound rule on the DMS security group that allows TCP 1521 to the on-premises database CIDR range.","An outbound rule on the DMS security group that allows TCP 3306 to the Aurora security group.","An inbound rule on the Aurora security group that allows TCP 3306 from the DMS security group.","An outbound rule on the Aurora security group that allows TCP 3306 to the DMS security group.","An inbound rule on the DMS security group that allows TCP 1521 from the on-premises database CIDR range.","An inbound rule on the Aurora security group that allows TCP 3306 from 0.0.0.0/0."],"a":[0,1,2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'removed the default allow all outbound rule'. Dalam skenario ini DMS replication instance adalah pihak yang menginisiasi kedua koneksi: ke Oracle on-premises (source) dan ke Aurora (target). Karena outbound default sudah dihapus, security group DMS harus punya outbound rule ke 1521 on-premises dan ke 3306 Aurora. Di sisi target, security group Aurora harus mengizinkan inbound 3306 dari security group DMS. Security group bersifat stateful, sehingga traffic balasan tidak memerlukan rule tambahan; itulah mengapa outbound dari Aurora atau inbound 1521 ke DMS tidak diperlukan. Membuka 3306 ke 0.0.0.0/0 berfungsi tetapi melanggar least privilege. Aturan umum: tentukan siapa yang menginisiasi koneksi, beri outbound di sisi inisiator dan inbound di sisi tujuan, lalu andalkan sifat stateful untuk traffic balasan.","r":["Benar — DMS menginisiasi koneksi ke Oracle on-premises, jadi tanpa outbound default rule ini wajib ada.","Benar — DMS menginisiasi koneksi ke Aurora, jadi outbound 3306 ke security group Aurora wajib ada.","Benar — Aurora harus menerima koneksi masuk dari DMS di port 3306.","Salah — Security group stateful, sehingga balasan dari Aurora ke DMS otomatis diizinkan tanpa outbound rule.","Salah — Database on-premises tidak menginisiasi koneksi ke DMS; balasan dari Oracle sudah diizinkan karena sifat stateful.","Salah — Membuka port database ke seluruh internet tidak perlu dan melanggar least privilege."],"k":"Tips ujian: security group stateful → rule hanya dibutuhkan di arah inisiasi koneksi (outbound di inisiator, inbound di tujuan)."},{"id":"E3B-30","d":3,"ts":"3.3.4","t":"Glue small files - file grouping","q":"An AWS Glue ETL job reads a partition that contains 2 million small JSON files (a few KB each) from Amazon S3. The job fails with driver out-of-memory errors, and Glue job metrics show high driver JVM heap usage while executors are mostly idle. Which change will MOST likely fix the issue with the LEAST effort?","o":["Enable file grouping on the S3 source by setting groupFiles to inPartition and a suitable groupSize.","Increase the number of workers from 10 to 50.","Switch the job to use the Python shell job type.","Disable continuous logging for the job."],"a":[0],"e":"Gejala kuncinya: 'millions of small files' dan 'driver out-of-memory' dengan executor idle. Driver Spark harus melacak metadata dan task untuk setiap file; jutaan file kecil membuat driver kehabisan memori. Opsi Glue groupFiles (inPartition) dan groupSize menggabungkan banyak file kecil menjadi grup yang dibaca satu task, sehingga jumlah task dan beban driver turun drastis. Distraktor terdekat adalah menambah worker: menambah executor, tetapi masalahnya ada di memori driver, bukan kapasitas executor. Python shell job tidak cocok untuk volume data terdistribusi. Continuous logging tidak memengaruhi memori driver. Aturan jangka panjang: kompaksi file kecil; perbaikan cepat di Glue: file grouping.","r":["Benar — File grouping menggabungkan file kecil sehingga jumlah task dan tekanan memori driver berkurang.","Salah — Menambah worker tidak mengurangi beban driver yang melacak jutaan file.","Salah — Python shell berjalan di satu mesin dan tidak cocok untuk volume data ini.","Salah — Logging tidak berhubungan dengan OOM pada driver."],"k":"Tips ujian: Glue + banyak file kecil + driver OOM → groupFiles/groupSize (atau kompaksi file)."},{"id":"E3B-09","d":3,"ts":"3.3.1","t":"Auditing Athena queries with CloudTrail","q":"A compliance policy requires that the company retain, for 1 year, a record of which IAM principal started each Amazon Athena query, when it was started, and its query execution ID. Analysts currently rely on the Athena console's Recent queries list. Which solution meets the requirement?","o":["Keep using the Athena query history in the console because it retains all queries indefinitely.","Enable Athena workgroup query result encryption and store results in S3 for 1 year.","Configure Amazon Managed Grafana with the Athena data source to display the query history.","Use a CloudTrail trail that captures management events, including StartQueryExecution, and deliver the logs to an S3 bucket with a 1-year retention policy."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'which IAM principal', 'when', dan 'for 1 year'. Setiap query Athena dimulai dengan panggilan API StartQueryExecution, yang dicatat CloudTrail sebagai management event lengkap dengan userIdentity, eventTime, dan responseElements.queryExecutionId. Dengan trail ke S3 plus lifecycle/retensi, catatan tersebut bertahan sesuai kebijakan. Distraktor terdekat adalah riwayat query di console Athena, tetapi Athena hanya menyimpan riwayat query selama 45 hari, jadi tidak memenuhi 1 tahun. Menyimpan hasil query (result set) tidak sama dengan mencatat siapa yang menjalankan query, dan Grafana hanya alat visualisasi. Perhatikan: demi keamanan, field queryString pada log CloudTrail StartQueryExecution berisi '***OMITTED***'; teks SQL hanya bisa diambil lewat API GetQueryExecution dengan queryExecutionId selama riwayat masih tersedia (45 hari), jadi jika teks SQL juga harus disimpan 1 tahun, perlu proses tambahan yang menyalinnya. Aturan: audit siapa memanggil layanan serverless → CloudTrail trail ke S3.","r":["Salah — Athena hanya menyimpan riwayat query di console selama 45 hari, tidak memenuhi retensi 1 tahun.","Salah — Enkripsi dan penyimpanan hasil query tidak mencatat principal yang menjalankan query.","Salah — Grafana adalah alat visualisasi dan tidak menciptakan catatan audit yang tahan lama.","Benar — CloudTrail merekam StartQueryExecution beserta userIdentity, eventTime, dan queryExecutionId, dan trail ke S3 memungkinkan retensi 1 tahun."],"k":"Tips ujian: riwayat Athena console = 45 hari; audit siapa menjalankan query jangka panjang → CloudTrail trail ke S3 (queryString di CloudTrail berisi ***OMITTED***)."},{"id":"E1C-69","d":1,"ts":"1.4.6","t":"AWS SAM templates","q":"A data engineer is building a serverless ingestion pipeline that consists of three AWS Lambda functions, an AWS Step Functions state machine, and an Amazon DynamoDB table. The engineer wants a concise template syntax for serverless resources, the ability to build and package the function code, and a single command to deploy the whole application through CloudFormation. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create the resources in the AWS Management Console and export their configuration.","Write an AWS SAM template that uses AWS::Serverless::Function, AWS::Serverless::StateMachine, and AWS::Serverless::SimpleTable resources, then run 'sam build' and 'sam deploy'.","Upload each function as a .zip file to Amazon S3 and create the state machine with the AWS CLI.","Use AWS CodeDeploy to deploy the DynamoDB table and the state machine."],"a":[1],"e":"Kebutuhannya: 'concise template syntax for serverless resources', 'build and package the function code', dan 'single command to deploy ... through CloudFormation'. AWS SAM adalah ekstensi CloudFormation (Transform: AWS::Serverless-2016-10-31) dengan resource ringkas seperti AWS::Serverless::Function, AWS::Serverless::StateMachine, dan AWS::Serverless::SimpleTable; 'sam build' menyiapkan dependensi dan artefak, dan 'sam deploy' mengunggah artefak lalu men-deploy stack CloudFormation. Distractor terdekat adalah unggah .zip dan CLI: bisa membuat resource, tetapi manual, tanpa template tunggal atau rollback. Konsol tidak repeatable. CodeDeploy menangani deployment aplikasi, bukan pembuatan tabel DynamoDB atau state machine. Aturan umum: package dan deploy aplikasi serverless (Lambda, Step Functions, DynamoDB) → AWS SAM.","r":["Salah — Pembuatan manual di konsol tidak repeatable.","Benar — SAM menyediakan sintaks ringkas, build/package, dan deploy via CloudFormation.","Salah — Langkah manual tanpa template tunggal, state, atau rollback.","Salah — CodeDeploy tidak membuat tabel DynamoDB atau state machine."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'package and deploy serverless app' → AWS SAM (sam build, sam deploy)."},{"id":"E3A-54","d":3,"ts":"3.2.3","t":"Redshift late-binding views","q":"A data engineer creates an external schema in Amazon Redshift that points to the AWS Glue Data Catalog and wants to create a view that joins a local Redshift table with a Redshift Spectrum external table. The CREATE VIEW statement fails. What should the data engineer do to create the view?","o":["Grant the Redshift cluster role the AWS Glue CreateTable permission.","Create a materialized view with AUTO REFRESH YES instead.","Copy the external table into a local table each night and build the view on the copy.","Add the WITH NO SCHEMA BINDING clause to make the view a late-binding view."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kuncinya adalah view yang mereferensikan 'Redshift Spectrum external table' dan pernyataan CREATE VIEW yang gagal. Di Amazon Redshift, view biasa terikat ke skema objek yang direferensikan, sedangkan tabel eksternal tidak bisa diikat seperti itu. View yang mereferensikan tabel eksternal harus dibuat sebagai late-binding view dengan klausa WITH NO SCHEMA BINDING, sehingga objek baru diperiksa saat query dijalankan. Izin CreateTable di Glue tidak relevan karena tabel eksternal sudah ada. Materialized view bukan perbaikan untuk kesalahan sintaks view, dan materialized view atas tabel eksternal punya keterbatasan dalam refresh. Menyalin data setiap malam menghilangkan manfaat Spectrum dan menambah pipeline. Aturan umum: view atas Spectrum external table → WITH NO SCHEMA BINDING.","r":["Salah — Tabel eksternal sudah ada; masalahnya ada pada schema binding view, bukan izin Glue.","Salah — Mengganti jenis objek tanpa alasan dan tidak menjawab penyebab kegagalan.","Salah — Menambah pipeline dan duplikasi data yang tidak perlu.","Benar — Late-binding view (WITH NO SCHEMA BINDING) wajib untuk view yang mereferensikan tabel eksternal."],"k":"Tips ujian: Redshift view atas tabel Spectrum/external → WITH NO SCHEMA BINDING (late-binding view)."},{"id":"E3A-09","d":3,"ts":"3.1.3","t":"Calling Athena with the SDK","q":"A Python application uses the AWS SDK for Python (Boto3) to run an Amazon Athena query. The code calls start_query_execution and immediately calls get_query_results with the returned QueryExecutionId. The call often fails with an error saying the query has not yet finished. How should the data engineer fix the code?","o":["Pass a larger timeout value to start_query_execution so that the call blocks until the query finishes.","Call get_query_execution in a loop until the query state is SUCCEEDED, FAILED, or CANCELLED, and call get_query_results only after the state is SUCCEEDED.","Replace Athena with an Amazon Redshift JDBC connection because Athena APIs do not return query results.","Call start_query_execution again with the same QueryExecutionId until results are returned."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya: start_query_execution bersifat asinkron, hanya mengembalikan QueryExecutionId lalu query berjalan di latar belakang. Pola SDK yang benar adalah mengecek status dengan get_query_execution (polling dengan jeda) sampai state menjadi SUCCEEDED, FAILED, atau CANCELLED. Setelah SUCCEEDED, ambil hasil dengan get_query_results (gunakan paginator untuk hasil besar) atau baca file hasil di S3 output location. Tidak ada parameter timeout yang membuat start_query_execution menjadi blocking. Athena API jelas mengembalikan hasil, jadi pindah ke Redshift tidak perlu. Memanggil start_query_execution lagi justru menjalankan query baru dan menambah biaya. Aturan umum: banyak API data AWS (Athena, Redshift Data API, Glue StartJobRun) asinkron, jadi pola standarnya start → cek status → ambil hasil.","r":["Salah — start_query_execution tidak punya mode blocking; ia selalu langsung mengembalikan ID.","Benar — Polling get_query_execution sampai selesai, lalu panggil get_query_results hanya jika SUCCEEDED.","Salah — Athena API mengembalikan hasil lewat get_query_results atau file di S3; tidak perlu ganti layanan.","Salah — Memanggil start lagi menjalankan query baru, menambah biaya, dan tidak menunggu query sebelumnya."],"k":"Tips ujian: API Athena asinkron → start_query_execution → get_query_execution (status) → get_query_results."},{"id":"E4B-32","d":4,"ts":"4.4.4","t":"CloudWatch Logs Insights","q":"An AWS Lambda function that processes order events writes its logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. A data engineer needs to quickly find the 10 most frequent error messages from the last hour to troubleshoot a failure. The engineer wants an interactive, ad hoc query without moving data. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Export the log group to Amazon S3 and query it with Amazon Athena.","Create a metric filter for the word ERROR and view the metric on a CloudWatch dashboard.","Stream the log group to Amazon OpenSearch Service and build a visualization in OpenSearch Dashboards.","Run a CloudWatch Logs Insights query on the log group that filters error messages, counts them by message, and sorts the results."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'interactive, ad hoc query', 'last hour', dan 'without moving data'. CloudWatch Logs Insights menjalankan query langsung di log group dengan perintah seperti filter, stats count(*) by @message, sort, dan limit, sehingga 10 pesan error terbanyak dapat ditemukan dalam hitungan detik tanpa memindahkan data. Distraktor terdekat adalah metric filter: hanya menghitung kemunculan pola untuk data yang masuk setelah filter dibuat dan tidak menampilkan teks pesan error yang paling sering. Export ke S3 + Athena memindahkan data dan butuh waktu. OpenSearch membutuhkan streaming dan cluster tambahan, berlebihan untuk troubleshooting ad hoc. Aturan umum: query ad hoc pada log yang sudah di CloudWatch Logs → CloudWatch Logs Insights.","r":["Salah — Export memindahkan data dan memakan waktu, bertentangan dengan kebutuhan cepat tanpa memindahkan data.","Salah — Metric filter hanya menghitung kemunculan ke depan dan tidak mengelompokkan teks pesan error.","Salah — OpenSearch memerlukan streaming dan cluster tambahan, berlebihan untuk analisis ad hoc.","Benar — Logs Insights menjalankan query agregasi interaktif langsung pada log group."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'ad hoc query on CloudWatch Logs' → CloudWatch Logs Insights."},{"id":"E1A-42","d":1,"ts":"1.1.7","t":"Lambda Kinesis ParallelizationFactor","q":"An AWS Lambda function consumes records from an Amazon Kinesis data stream with 10 shards. The IteratorAge metric keeps growing during peak hours, but the function itself completes each batch quickly and the team cannot change the number of shards. Ordering must be preserved per partition key. What should the data engineer do to increase processing throughput?","o":["Increase the ParallelizationFactor on the event source mapping.","Decrease the batch size to 1 record.","Configure a dead-letter queue on the function.","Change the starting position to LATEST."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'IteratorAge keeps growing' (consumer tertinggal), 'cannot change the number of shards', dan 'ordering must be preserved per partition key'. Secara default Lambda memproses satu batch per shard pada satu waktu. ParallelizationFactor (1 sampai 10) memungkinkan beberapa batch dari shard yang sama diproses bersamaan, dan Lambda tetap menjaga urutan per partition key. Ini menaikkan throughput tanpa menambah shard. Distraktor terdekat adalah memperkecil batch size: menambah jumlah invocation dan overhead, sehingga throughput turun. DLQ hanya menangani kegagalan. Mengubah starting position ke LATEST berarti melewatkan record yang belum diproses. Aturan umum: Lambda tertinggal pada Kinesis tanpa resharding = naikkan ParallelizationFactor (maks 10).","r":["Benar — ParallelizationFactor memproses beberapa batch per shard secara paralel sambil menjaga urutan per partition key.","Salah — Batch size 1 menambah jumlah invocation dan menurunkan throughput.","Salah — DLQ hanya menangkap kegagalan, tidak menambah throughput.","Salah — LATEST hanya berlaku saat mapping dibuat dan akan melewatkan record yang belum diproses."],"k":"Kinesis + Lambda IteratorAge naik, shard tetap → ParallelizationFactor (1–10)."},{"id":"E1A-18","d":1,"ts":"1.1.3","t":"AWS Glue small files grouping","q":"An AWS Glue ETL job reads an Amazon S3 prefix that contains about 2 million small JSON files (10 KB to 50 KB each). The job runs slowly and the driver sometimes runs out of memory while listing and tracking files. Which change should the data engineer make with the LEAST effort?","o":["Enable file grouping by setting groupFiles to inPartition and specifying a groupSize in the S3 connection options.","Increase the worker type to G.2X and double the number of workers.","Rewrite the job as an AWS Lambda function that processes one file at a time.","Enable AWS Glue job bookmarks."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: '2 million small JSON files' dan driver 'runs out of memory while listing and tracking files'. Banyak file kecil membuat Spark membuat satu task per file sehingga driver kewalahan melacak task dan metadata. Opsi groupFiles = inPartition dengan groupSize membuat Glue menggabungkan banyak file kecil menjadi satu grup baca, sehingga jumlah task turun drastis dan memori driver lega. Distraktor terdekat adalah memperbesar worker: biaya naik tetapi akar masalah (terlalu banyak task kecil) tetap ada. Lambda per file tidak praktis untuk 2 juta file dan transformasi set. Job bookmarks hanya mencegah file lama dibaca ulang, tidak mengatasi banyaknya file pada satu run. Aturan umum: small files problem di Glue = groupFiles/groupSize (dan jangka panjang, compaction di sumber).","r":["Benar — Pengelompokan file kecil mengurangi jumlah task dan beban memori driver dengan perubahan minimal.","Salah — Menambah kapasitas menaikkan biaya tanpa memperbaiki jumlah task yang berlebihan.","Salah — Menulis ulang ke Lambda per file butuh effort besar dan tidak efisien untuk jutaan file.","Salah — Bookmarks hanya melacak data yang sudah diproses, tidak mengatasi small files dalam satu run."],"k":"Glue + jutaan file kecil → groupFiles='inPartition' + groupSize."},{"id":"E1B-43","d":1,"ts":"1.2.6","t":"Firehose format conversion input requirements","q":"A company streams CSV-formatted log lines into Amazon Data Firehose and wants Firehose to deliver the data to Amazon S3 as Apache Parquet. When the data engineer tries to enable record format conversion, the conversion fails for every record. Which solution will resolve the issue?","o":["Add a Firehose data transformation Lambda function that converts each CSV record to JSON before record format conversion.","Increase the Firehose buffer size to the maximum value.","Change the output format of the record format conversion from Parquet to ORC.","Enable dynamic partitioning on the Firehose stream."],"a":[0],"e":"Petunjuk kuncinya adalah input berupa 'CSV-formatted log lines' dan konversi gagal 'for every record'. Record format conversion di Firehose hanya menerima input JSON, sehingga data non-JSON seperti CSV harus terlebih dahulu diubah ke JSON melalui fungsi Lambda transformation yang terpasang di Firehose, lalu baru diserialisasi ke Parquet dengan skema dari Glue Data Catalog. Menaikkan buffer size tidak mengubah format input. Mengganti output ke ORC tidak membantu karena masalahnya ada pada format input, bukan output. Dynamic partitioning hanya mengatur prefix tujuan di S3. Aturan umum: Firehose format conversion butuh JSON; selain JSON → tambahkan Lambda transformation terlebih dahulu.","r":["Benar — Lambda mengubah CSV menjadi JSON sehingga record format conversion dapat menghasilkan Parquet.","Salah — Ukuran buffer tidak memengaruhi format input yang tidak didukung.","Salah — ORC juga membutuhkan input JSON; masalahnya tetap ada.","Salah — Dynamic partitioning mengatur prefix S3, bukan konversi format."],"k":"Tips ujian: Firehose record format conversion hanya menerima JSON → CSV/log harus diubah ke JSON dengan Lambda dulu."},{"id":"E1C-56","d":1,"ts":"1.4.4","t":"Git revert vs reset","q":"A data engineer merged and pushed a commit to the shared main branch of the team's Git repository. The commit introduced a bug into an AWS Glue job script, and the CI/CD pipeline already deployed it. Several teammates have since pulled main. The engineer must undo the change quickly while keeping the repository history intact for everyone. What should the engineer do?","o":["Run git reset --hard to the previous commit and force-push main.","Run git revert on the faulty commit, push the new commit to main, and let the pipeline redeploy.","Delete the main branch and recreate it from a teammate's local copy.","Edit the deployed script directly in the AWS Glue console and leave the repository unchanged."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'shared main branch', 'teammates have since pulled', dan 'keeping the repository history intact'. git revert membuat commit baru yang membalik perubahan commit bermasalah tanpa menulis ulang riwayat, sehingga aman untuk branch bersama; setelah di-push, pipeline CI/CD men-deploy versi yang sudah diperbaiki. Distractor terdekat adalah git reset --hard + force push: memang menghapus commit, tetapi menulis ulang riwayat yang sudah dipakai rekan, menyebabkan konflik dan potensi hilangnya pekerjaan mereka. Mengedit langsung di konsol menciptakan drift antara repositori dan produksi, dan deployment berikutnya akan memunculkan bug lagi. Menghapus branch main berisiko dan tidak perlu. Aturan umum: undo di branch bersama → git revert; reset/force-push hanya untuk branch lokal yang belum dibagikan.","r":["Salah — Menulis ulang riwayat branch bersama mengganggu rekan dan berisiko kehilangan commit.","Benar — Revert menambahkan commit pembalik yang aman dan memicu redeploy melalui pipeline.","Salah — Tindakan ekstrem yang berisiko dan menghapus riwayat.","Salah — Membuat drift; deployment berikutnya dari repo akan mengembalikan bug."],"k":"Tips ujian: undo commit yang sudah di-push ke shared branch → git revert (bukan reset + force push)."},{"id":"E4B-43","d":4,"ts":"4.5.2","t":"Amazon Macie automated discovery","q":"A company has more than 2,000 Amazon S3 buckets across multiple accounts. The privacy office wants continuous, cost-efficient visibility into which buckets are likely to contain personally identifiable information (PII) such as names, addresses, and credit card numbers, without having to configure and schedule individual scan jobs for each bucket. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Run AWS Glue crawlers on all buckets and review the inferred classifications.","Enable Amazon GuardDuty S3 Protection in every account.","Enable Amazon Inspector for all accounts.","Enable Amazon Macie with automated sensitive data discovery for the organization."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: PII di '2,000 Amazon S3 buckets', 'continuous, cost-efficient', dan tanpa 'configure and schedule individual scan jobs'. Amazon Macie memakai machine learning dan pattern matching (managed data identifiers) untuk menemukan data sensitif di S3; fitur automated sensitive data discovery secara otomatis dan berkelanjutan mengambil sampel objek di seluruh bucket dan memberikan sensitivity score per bucket, sehingga hemat biaya tanpa membuat job satu per satu. Dengan delegated administrator, Macie dapat diaktifkan untuk seluruh organisasi. Distraktor terdekat adalah Glue crawler: crawler menyimpulkan skema dan format, bukan mendeteksi PII di isi data. GuardDuty S3 Protection mendeteksi aktivitas mencurigakan (ancaman), bukan isi sensitif. Inspector memindai kerentanan software pada EC2, container, dan Lambda. Aturan umum: 'discover PII/sensitive data in S3' → Amazon Macie (automated sensitive data discovery).","r":["Salah — Crawler menyimpulkan skema, bukan mengidentifikasi PII di isi objek.","Salah — GuardDuty mendeteksi ancaman dan aktivitas anomali, bukan data sensitif.","Salah — Inspector memindai kerentanan software, bukan isi data di S3.","Benar — Macie automated sensitive data discovery memindai bucket secara berkelanjutan dan hemat biaya."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'PII discovery in S3 at scale' → Macie automated sensitive data discovery."},{"id":"E2A-37","d":2,"ts":"2.1.4","t":"Integrating Transfer Family into pipelines","q":"Thirty vendors upload inventory files once per day. Vendors can only use SFTP. As soon as a file arrives, an AWS Glue job must transform it and load it into Amazon Redshift. The company wants a serverless, event-driven design with the LEAST operational overhead. Which TWO actions should a data engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Create an AWS Transfer Family SFTP server that stores uploaded files in an Amazon S3 bucket.","Run an SFTP daemon on an Amazon EC2 instance and use a cron job to start the AWS Glue job every hour.","Enable Amazon EventBridge notifications on the S3 bucket and create a rule for Object Created events that starts an AWS Step Functions workflow that runs the AWS Glue job.","Install AWS DataSync agents at each vendor site to copy files to Amazon S3.","Order an AWS Snowball Edge device for each vendor and import the files into Amazon S3 weekly."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'Vendors can only use SFTP', 'as soon as a file arrives', dan 'serverless, event-driven ... LEAST operational overhead'. AWS Transfer Family menyediakan endpoint SFTP managed yang langsung menulis file ke S3, sehingga tidak ada server yang dikelola. Integrasi S3 dengan Amazon EventBridge memancarkan event Object Created, dan rule EventBridge dapat memulai workflow Step Functions yang menjalankan Glue job, sehingga pipeline bersifat event-driven tanpa polling. Distraktor terdekat adalah SFTP di EC2 dengan cron: memenuhi protokol, tetapi ada server yang harus dikelola dan pemrosesan tidak segera (menunggu jadwal). DataSync membutuhkan agent di lokasi vendor dan Snowball adalah transfer offline untuk volume besar, keduanya tidak cocok untuk unggahan harian dari pihak luar. Aturan umum: integrasikan alat migrasi/transfer ke pipeline dengan menjadikan landing S3 sebagai pemicu event (EventBridge) untuk orkestrasi.","r":["Benar — Transfer Family memberi endpoint SFTP serverless yang menyimpan file langsung di S3 sebagai landing zone.","Salah — Server EC2 harus dikelola dan cron per jam tidak memproses file segera setelah tiba.","Benar — Event Object Created melalui EventBridge memicu Step Functions dan Glue secara otomatis tanpa polling.","Salah — Vendor eksternal tidak menjalankan agent DataSync dan hanya bisa memakai SFTP.","Salah — Snowball adalah transfer offline untuk volume besar, tidak cocok untuk file harian dan menambah keterlambatan."],"k":"SFTP from partners → Transfer Family → S3 → EventBridge → Step Functions/Glue (event-driven)."},{"id":"E2B-31","d":2,"ts":"2.3.1","t":"Redshift UNLOAD to Parquet","q":"A company keeps 5 years of order history in Amazon Redshift, but only the last 12 months are queried often. To reduce cluster storage, the company wants to move older data to Amazon S3 in a format that Amazon Athena and Redshift Spectrum can query efficiently with filters on order year and month. Which solution meets these requirements MOST efficiently?","o":["Use a SQL client to SELECT the old rows into CSV files on an Amazon EC2 instance, and upload the files to Amazon S3.","Run an UNLOAD command with FORMAT AS PARQUET and PARTITION BY (order_year, order_month) to Amazon S3, catalog the output, and then delete the unloaded rows from the Redshift table.","Take a manual snapshot of the cluster and restore only the old tables when they are needed.","Run UNLOAD to CSV without partitions, and then run an AWS Glue job to convert the files to partitioned Parquet."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'move older data to Amazon S3', 'query efficiently with filters on order year and month' dan 'MOST efficiently'. UNLOAD menulis hasil query Redshift ke S3 secara paralel; dengan FORMAT AS PARQUET hasilnya kolumnar dan terkompresi, dan dengan PARTITION BY data tersusun dalam folder Hive-style yang memungkinkan partition pruning di Athena dan Spectrum. Setelah output di-catalog dan baris lama dihapus, ini menjadi pola hot di Redshift dan cold di S3. Unload ke CSV lalu konversi dengan Glue berfungsi, tetapi menambah job dan salinan data. Ekspor lewat SQL client lambat dan tidak paralel. Snapshot tidak bisa di-query langsung dan butuh restore. Ingat: Redshift → S3 untuk data lake → UNLOAD ... FORMAT PARQUET PARTITION BY.","r":["Salah — Ekspor lewat SQL client tidak paralel, lambat untuk data besar, dan menghasilkan CSV yang mahal di-query.","Benar — UNLOAD ke Parquet berpartisi menghasilkan data S3 yang efisien untuk Athena dan Spectrum dalam satu langkah.","Salah — Snapshot tidak bisa di-query dari S3 dan harus di-restore terlebih dahulu.","Salah — Langkah konversi tambahan menambah biaya dan kompleksitas dibandingkan UNLOAD langsung ke Parquet berpartisi."],"k":"Tips ujian: arsipkan data Redshift ke S3 untuk query → UNLOAD FORMAT AS PARQUET PARTITION BY."},{"id":"E2C-08","d":2,"ts":"2.4.1","t":"Lake Formation catalog design with LF-Tags","q":"A company is building a data lake on Amazon S3 governed by AWS Lake Formation. It has raw, curated, and analytics zones across 12 business domains, with more than 4,000 tables. Access must be granted according to data classification (public, internal, confidential) and domain, and new tables must inherit the correct permissions automatically without per-table grants. How should the data engineer design the catalog and permissions?","o":["Create one AWS Glue Data Catalog database per zone and domain, define LF-Tags such as domain and classification, assign the tags to databases and sensitive columns, and grant permissions on LF-Tag expressions.","Create one database for all 4,000 tables and grant named-resource permissions on each table to each IAM role.","Store each domain in a separate S3 bucket and manage access only with S3 bucket policies, bypassing the Data Catalog.","Create a separate AWS account for each classification level and copy tables between accounts when access is needed."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah 'more than 4,000 tables' dan 'new tables must inherit the correct permissions automatically'. Desain yang skalabel di AWS Lake Formation adalah mengorganisir Glue Data Catalog per zone/domain dan memakai LF-Tags (tag-based access control/LF-TBAC). Tag yang dipasang di level database diwariskan ke tabel dan kolom di dalamnya, dan izin diberikan berdasarkan ekspresi tag (misalnya domain=finance AND classification=internal), sehingga tabel baru otomatis mendapat izin yang tepat. Named-resource grant per tabel untuk ribuan tabel tidak skalabel dan rawan kesalahan. Bucket policy S3 tidak memberikan kontrol di level kolom/tabel dan mem-bypass governance Lake Formation. Menyalin data antar akun menciptakan duplikasi dan overhead sinkronisasi. Aturan umum: banyak tabel + izin berdasarkan atribut → LF-Tags dengan pewarisan dari database.","r":["Benar — Database per zone/domain plus LF-Tags yang diwariskan memungkinkan izin otomatis berdasarkan ekspresi tag untuk tabel baru.","Salah — Grant per tabel untuk ribuan tabel tidak skalabel dan tidak otomatis berlaku untuk tabel baru.","Salah — Bucket policy tidak mendukung izin per kolom/tabel dan mengabaikan governance Lake Formation.","Salah — Menyalin tabel antar akun menimbulkan duplikasi data dan overhead operasional."],"k":"Tips ujian: Lake Formation dengan ribuan tabel / izin berbasis klasifikasi → LF-Tags (LF-TBAC), bukan named-resource grants."},{"id":"E1C-78","d":1,"ts":"1.4.11","t":"Graph data structures for lineage","q":"A company has 3,000 datasets produced by Glue jobs, Amazon Redshift views, and dashboards. Each dataset can have multiple upstream sources and multiple downstream consumers, with chains up to 15 levels deep. Before changing a source table, data engineers must quickly find every downstream dataset that could be affected. Which approach is the MOST appropriate?","o":["Store each dataset as a row in a relational table with a single parent_id column and query it with a fixed number of self-joins.","Store the lineage as a list of dataset names in a single JSON file in Amazon S3 and search it with a text search.","Model the lineage as a directed graph (datasets as vertices, data flows as edges) in Amazon Neptune and run a graph traversal that follows outgoing edges from the source table.","Store each dataset in Amazon DynamoDB with the dataset name as the partition key and look up each consumer one at a time manually."],"a":[2],"e":"Kebutuhannya: hubungan banyak-ke-banyak ('multiple upstream ... multiple downstream'), rantai hingga '15 levels deep', dan menemukan 'every downstream dataset' dengan cepat. Lineage secara alami adalah directed graph (umumnya DAG): dataset sebagai vertex dan aliran data sebagai edge berarah. Analisis dampak adalah traversal graf (BFS/DFS) mengikuti edge keluar dari tabel sumber, yang efisien di database graf seperti Amazon Neptune dengan query Gremlin, openCypher, atau SPARQL. Distractor terdekat adalah tabel relasional dengan parent_id: struktur pohon dengan satu parent tidak dapat merepresentasikan banyak upstream, dan self-join dengan jumlah tetap tidak menjangkau kedalaman yang bervariasi. File JSON dan pencarian teks tidak memodelkan hubungan. Lookup DynamoDB manual satu per satu lambat dan rawan terlewat. Aturan umum: hubungan many-to-many yang dalam (lineage, dependency) → struktur data graph dan traversal; database graph → Neptune.","r":["Salah — Satu parent_id hanya memodelkan pohon dan self-join tetap tidak menjangkau kedalaman bervariasi.","Salah — Pencarian teks tidak bisa menelusuri hubungan bertingkat.","Benar — Directed graph dengan traversal edge keluar menemukan semua dataset hilir secara efisien.","Salah — Lookup manual per item lambat dan tidak menelusuri graf secara otomatis."],"k":"Tips ujian: lineage / impact analysis / many-to-many relationships → graph (DAG) + traversal (Neptune)."},{"id":"E4A-56","d":4,"ts":"4.2.6","t":"IAM Access Analyzer policy generation","q":"An IAM role used by an Amazon EMR pipeline was created a year ago with broad permissions (s3:*, glue:*, and dynamodb:*) on all resources. The pipeline has run in production since then, and AWS CloudTrail is enabled. The security team wants to replace the policy with a least-privilege policy that is based on the actions and resources the pipeline actually used, with the LEAST effort. Which solution meets this requirement?","o":["Use IAM Access Analyzer policy generation to create a policy from the role's CloudTrail activity, review it, and replace the broad policy.","Remove all permissions from the role and add permissions back one at a time as the pipeline fails.","Attach the AWS managed policies AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess and AWSGlueConsoleFullAccess instead of the custom policy.","Ask the developers to list from memory the APIs that the pipeline calls."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'based on the actions and resources the pipeline actually used' dan 'LEAST effort'. IAM Access Analyzer dapat menghasilkan policy berdasarkan aktivitas yang tercatat di CloudTrail untuk role tertentu dalam rentang waktu yang dipilih. Hasilnya berisi action dan, untuk banyak service, resource yang benar-benar dipakai, sehingga tinggal ditinjau dan disesuaikan sebelum menggantikan policy lama. Mencabut semua izin lalu menambah satu per satu menyebabkan gangguan produksi. Managed policy umum tetap terlalu luas atau malah kurang (misalnya tidak mencakup DynamoDB). Mengandalkan ingatan developer tidak akurat. Aturan umum: right-sizing permission dari aktivitas nyata → IAM Access Analyzer policy generation (dan last accessed information).","r":["Benar — Access Analyzer membuat policy dari aktivitas CloudTrail nyata sehingga mendekati least privilege dengan usaha minimal.","Salah — Menyebabkan kegagalan produksi berulang dan sangat lambat.","Salah — Managed policy ini tidak sesuai dengan kebutuhan aktual dan tetap terlalu luas.","Salah — Tidak akurat dan tidak dapat diverifikasi."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'generate least-privilege policy from actual usage' → IAM Access Analyzer policy generation (CloudTrail)."},{"id":"E2B-55","d":2,"ts":"2.3.6","t":"S3 Cross-Region Replication with RTC","q":"A company's data lake in us-east-1 must remain available if the entire Region becomes unavailable. The business requires that 99.99% of new objects be copied to us-west-2 within 15 minutes, with metrics and notifications for objects that are late. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Configure S3 Same-Region Replication with S3 Replication Time Control.","Create an AWS Backup plan that backs up the bucket to us-west-2 once a day.","Enable versioning on both buckets and configure S3 Cross-Region Replication to us-west-2 with S3 Replication Time Control (S3 RTC) enabled.","Run an hourly AWS DataSync task that copies new objects to us-west-2."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'entire Region becomes unavailable', '99.99% of new objects ... within 15 minutes' dan 'metrics and notifications'. Cross-Region Replication (CRR) menyalin objek ke bucket di Region lain; mensyaratkan versioning di bucket sumber dan tujuan. S3 Replication Time Control menambahkan SLA bahwa 99,99% objek direplikasi dalam 15 menit, plus replication metrics dan event notifications untuk objek yang terlambat. Same-Region Replication tetap di Region yang sama sehingga tidak melindungi dari kegagalan Region. Backup harian dan DataSync per jam tidak memenuhi target 15 menit. Ingat: 'replicate within 15 minutes with SLA' → CRR + S3 RTC; tanpa SLA → CRR biasa.","r":["Salah — SRR tetap di Region yang sama, sehingga tidak melindungi dari kegagalan Region.","Salah — Backup harian memberi RPO hingga 24 jam, jauh di atas 15 menit.","Benar — CRR dengan RTC memberi SLA 15 menit, metrik dan notifikasi, dan melindungi dari kegagalan Region.","Salah — DataSync per jam tidak memenuhi target 15 menit dan menambah penjadwalan."],"k":"Tips ujian: '15 minutes' + 'replication SLA' → S3 Replication Time Control (dengan CRR untuk DR lintas Region)."},{"id":"E1C-44","d":1,"ts":"1.3.1","t":"Glue workflow run properties","q":"An AWS Glue workflow runs job A, which determines the business date of the data it loaded, followed by job B and job C, which must use the same business date. Currently each job recalculates the date, and sometimes they disagree. How should the data engineer share the value across the jobs in the same workflow run with the LEAST effort?","o":["Write the date to a file on the Glue driver's local disk in job A and read it in jobs B and C.","Hardcode the date as a default job parameter and update it every day.","Store the date in an environment variable of job A.","In job A, set the business date as a workflow run property by calling PutWorkflowRunProperties, and read it in jobs B and C with GetWorkflowRunProperties."],"a":[3],"e":"Kebutuhannya: berbagi satu nilai antar job 'in the same workflow run' dengan 'LEAST effort'. Glue workflow memiliki run properties, yaitu pasangan key-value yang dibagikan ke semua job dalam satu workflow run; job A dapat menulisnya dengan PutWorkflowRunProperties dan job berikutnya membacanya dengan GetWorkflowRunProperties menggunakan WORKFLOW_NAME dan WORKFLOW_RUN_ID yang diteruskan otomatis. Distractor terdekat adalah file di disk lokal driver: setiap job berjalan di lingkungan terpisah yang hilang setelah job selesai, jadi file tidak dapat dibaca job lain. Hardcode parameter harian adalah pekerjaan manual. Environment variable hanya hidup di proses job A. Aturan umum: berbagi state antar job dalam Glue workflow → workflow run properties.","r":["Salah — Disk lokal setiap job bersifat sementara dan tidak dapat diakses job lain.","Salah — Pembaruan manual harian rawan kesalahan.","Salah — Environment variable tidak berpindah antar job.","Benar — Run properties dibagikan ke semua job dalam satu workflow run."],"k":"Tips ujian: share parameters between jobs in a Glue workflow → workflow run properties."},{"id":"E1B-51","d":1,"ts":"1.2.7","t":"Debugging AWS Glue jobs","q":"An AWS Glue Spark ETL job fails intermittently with an error at a late stage, and the default error message in the console is not detailed enough to identify the cause. The data engineer must find which stage and which executor failed and why. Which TWO actions should the data engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Enable AWS CloudTrail data events for the source S3 bucket.","Increase the job timeout value.","Enable continuous logging for the job and review the driver and executor logs in Amazon CloudWatch Logs.","Create AWS Config rules to track changes to the Glue job.","Enable the Spark UI for the job (with event logs stored in Amazon S3) and use Glue job run insights to analyze the failing stage and tasks."],"a":[2,4],"e":"Penentunya adalah kebutuhan mengetahui 'which stage and which executor failed and why' untuk job Spark. Continuous logging mengirim log driver dan executor ke CloudWatch Logs secara real time sehingga stack trace dan pesan error spesifik terlihat. Spark UI (dengan event log di S3) memperlihatkan DAG, stage, task, shuffle, dan executor yang gagal, sementara job run insights menyorot baris skrip dan penyebab kegagalan yang mungkin. CloudTrail hanya mencatat panggilan API, tidak menjelaskan kegagalan di dalam Spark. Menaikkan timeout tidak membantu jika job gagal karena error, bukan karena waktu habis. AWS Config hanya melacak perubahan konfigurasi resource. Aturan umum: debug job Glue → CloudWatch Logs (continuous logging) + Spark UI/job run insights.","r":["Salah — CloudTrail mencatat panggilan API, bukan detail kegagalan stage atau executor Spark.","Salah — Job gagal karena error, bukan karena timeout.","Benar — Log driver dan executor di CloudWatch Logs menampilkan stack trace dan pesan error rinci.","Salah — AWS Config melacak perubahan konfigurasi, bukan error runtime.","Benar — Spark UI dan job run insights menunjukkan stage, task, dan executor yang gagal beserta penyebabnya."],"k":"Tips ujian: troubleshooting Glue → continuous logging (CloudWatch Logs), Spark UI, job run insights, job metrics."},{"id":"E2B-08","d":2,"ts":"2.2.3","t":"Glue crawler incremental crawls","q":"An AWS Glue crawler runs every night on an S3 bucket that contains 6 years of Parquet data partitioned as s3://lake/events/dt=YYYY-MM-DD/. Each night only one new dt= folder is added, and the schema rarely changes. The crawler now takes more than 3 hours and its cost keeps growing because it lists and samples the entire bucket. Which change will reduce crawler run time and cost MOST effectively?","o":["Configure the crawler's recrawl policy to crawl new folders only (incremental crawl).","Split the bucket into six crawlers, one for each year of data, and run them in parallel every night.","Run the crawler every hour instead of once a night so that each run has less work.","Delete the table from the Data Catalog before each run so that the crawler creates it fresh."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'only one new dt= folder is added', 'schema rarely changes', dan crawler 'lists and samples the entire bucket'. Recrawl policy 'Crawl new folders only' (incremental crawl) membuat crawler hanya memproses folder S3 yang baru sejak run terakhir dan menambahkan partisi baru ke tabel yang ada. Ini memotong waktu dan biaya secara drastis karena 6 tahun data lama tidak dipindai ulang. Memecah menjadi enam crawler paralel mungkin mempercepat, tetapi total data yang dipindai sama sehingga biaya tidak turun. Menjalankan tiap jam justru menambah jumlah full crawl. Menghapus tabel sebelum crawl membuat semua partisi harus ditemukan ulang. Ingat: pola partisi baru append-only + skema stabil → incremental crawl (atau S3 event-based crawl).","r":["Benar — Incremental crawl hanya memproses folder baru sehingga run time dan biaya turun drastis.","Salah — Paralelisme tidak mengurangi total data yang dipindai, jadi biaya tetap tinggi dan pengelolaan bertambah.","Salah — Setiap run tetap full crawl, sehingga frekuensi lebih tinggi malah menaikkan biaya.","Salah — Menghapus tabel memaksa crawler menemukan ulang semua partisi dan bisa memutus query yang sedang berjalan."],"k":"Tips ujian: crawler lambat pada data append-only → 'Crawl new folders only' atau S3 event mode."},{"id":"E1B-65","d":1,"ts":"1.2.10","t":"Bedrock batch inference for data processing","q":"An e-commerce company wants to generate a short summary and a sentiment label for about 3 million product reviews collected each day by using a foundation model on Amazon Bedrock. Results are needed by the next morning, and there is no real-time requirement. The company wants the MOST cost-effective approach with the LEAST custom orchestration. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Invoke the model synchronously from an AWS Lambda function for each review as it arrives, with reserved concurrency.","Purchase Provisioned Throughput for the model and call it from an always-on Amazon EC2 fleet.","Write the reviews as JSONL prompt records to Amazon S3 and submit an Amazon Bedrock batch inference job that writes the outputs to S3.","Deploy an open-source LLM on an Amazon SageMaker AI real-time endpoint and call it from an AWS Glue job."],"a":[2],"e":"Penentunya adalah volume besar ('about 3 million product reviews'), hasil cukup 'by the next morning' tanpa kebutuhan real-time, serta 'MOST cost-effective' dengan orkestrasi minimal. Amazon Bedrock batch inference memproses kumpulan prompt dalam file JSONL di S3 secara asinkron dan menulis hasilnya kembali ke S3, dengan harga yang lebih rendah daripada inferensi on-demand untuk model yang didukung, dan tanpa perlu menangani throttling per request. Pemanggilan sinkron per review dari Lambda adalah distraktor terdekat; itu berfungsi, tetapi lebih mahal dan rawan throttling serta membutuhkan logika retry. Provisioned Throughput dan EC2 always-on membayar kapasitas tetap. Endpoint SageMaker AI dengan model sendiri menambah pengelolaan infrastruktur dan biaya instance. Aturan umum: pemrosesan LLM massal yang tidak mendesak → Bedrock batch inference.","r":["Salah — Pemanggilan on-demand per review lebih mahal, rawan throttling, dan butuh logika retry.","Salah — Provisioned Throughput dan EC2 always-on membayar kapasitas tetap yang tidak perlu untuk beban harian.","Benar — Batch inference memproses JSONL di S3 secara asinkron dengan biaya lebih rendah dan orkestrasi minimal.","Salah — Hosting model sendiri di endpoint real-time menambah biaya instance dan pengelolaan."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'large volume LLM processing, not real-time, lowest cost' → Amazon Bedrock batch inference (JSONL in S3)."},{"id":"E1C-32","d":1,"ts":"1.3.3","t":"Step Functions Parallel vs Map","q":"After raw data lands, a serverless pipeline must run three independent transformations (sales, inventory, and returns), each implemented as a separate AWS Lambda function. A final step must combine their results only after all three finish. The total runtime should be as short as possible. Which Step Functions design meets these requirements?","o":["Use a Parallel state with three branches, one for each Lambda function, followed by an aggregation task.","Chain the three Lambda tasks one after another and then run the aggregation task.","Use a Choice state that selects one of the three Lambda functions based on the input.","Use a Map state that iterates over the three function names with MaxConcurrency set to 1."],"a":[0],"e":"Kebutuhannya: tiga transformasi 'independent' yang berbeda, digabung 'only after all three finish', dengan runtime 'as short as possible'. Parallel state menjalankan cabang berbeda secara bersamaan dan baru melanjutkan setelah semua cabang selesai, dengan output berupa array hasil tiap cabang untuk langkah agregasi. Distractor terdekat adalah merangkai secara berurutan: hasilnya benar, tetapi total waktu menjadi jumlah ketiganya, bukan yang terlama. Choice hanya memilih satu cabang. Map dengan MaxConcurrency 1 sama dengan berurutan, dan Map lebih cocok untuk logika yang sama atas banyak item. Aturan umum: cabang berbeda yang berjalan bersamaan → Parallel; logika sama untuk banyak item → Map.","r":["Benar — Parallel menjalankan ketiga cabang bersamaan dan menunggu semuanya sebelum agregasi.","Salah — Eksekusi berurutan memperpanjang total waktu.","Salah — Choice hanya menjalankan satu cabang.","Salah — Map dengan konkurensi 1 berjalan berurutan dan kurang tepat untuk logika berbeda."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'different independent tasks at the same time, then join' → Parallel state."},{"id":"E4B-20","d":4,"ts":"4.3.4","t":"Client-side encryption before transit","q":"A financial company uploads daily transaction files from its on-premises data center to Amazon S3. Regulations require that the data be encrypted before it leaves the company's network so that it is never transmitted or stored in plaintext outside the data center. The company wants to use AWS KMS to manage the keys. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Upload the files over HTTPS and enable default SSE-KMS encryption on the bucket.","Establish an AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection and upload the files through the VPN tunnel.","Use AWS DataSync to transfer the files, because DataSync encrypts data in transit with TLS.","Encrypt each file on premises with the Amazon S3 Encryption Client (or the AWS Encryption SDK) using a KMS key as the wrapping key, and then upload the encrypted files."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'encrypted before it leaves the company's network' dan 'never transmitted or stored in plaintext outside the data center'. Ini adalah client-side encryption (encryption before transit): file dienkripsi di on-premises dengan Amazon S3 Encryption Client atau AWS Encryption SDK memakai envelope encryption, dengan KMS key sebagai kunci pembungkus data key. AWS hanya menerima dan menyimpan ciphertext, sementara KMS tetap mengelola kunci dan mengaudit penggunaannya. Distraktor terdekat adalah HTTPS + SSE-KMS: data terenkripsi saat transit dan at rest, tetapi S3 menerima plaintext di sisi server sebelum mengenkripsinya, sehingga melanggar syarat. VPN dan DataSync hanya mengenkripsi saluran transmisi; data didekripsi di ujung tujuan sebelum disimpan. Aturan umum: 'encrypt before upload / AWS never sees plaintext' → client-side encryption.","r":["Salah — Data tiba di S3 dalam plaintext sebelum dienkripsi server-side, melanggar syarat.","Salah — VPN hanya mengenkripsi tunnel; data didekripsi saat keluar dari tunnel.","Salah — TLS DataSync melindungi transit saja; objek tetap diterima dalam plaintext oleh layanan.","Benar — Client-side encryption memastikan hanya ciphertext yang meninggalkan data center, dengan kunci dikelola KMS."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'encrypt before transit / before it leaves premises' → client-side encryption (S3 Encryption Client / Encryption SDK)."},{"id":"E3B-20","d":3,"ts":"3.3.3","t":"Amazon Redshift event notifications","q":"A data engineer needs to notify the analytics team whenever their Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster has a scheduled maintenance event, a node replacement, or a failed snapshot. The engineer wants to use a built-in Redshift feature and avoid custom code. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create a CloudWatch alarm on the CPUUtilization metric of the cluster.","Create a Lambda function that calls DescribeEvents every 10 minutes and emails new events.","Create an Amazon Redshift event notification subscription for the relevant event categories that publishes to an Amazon SNS topic.","Enable Redshift audit logging and send the user activity log to CloudWatch Logs."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'built-in Redshift feature' dan jenis kejadian 'maintenance', 'node replacement', 'failed snapshot'. Amazon Redshift event notifications memungkinkan Anda membuat subscription berdasarkan kategori (management, monitoring, security, pending) dan severity, yang dipublikasikan ke SNS topic. Distraktor terdekat adalah Lambda polling DescribeEvents — bisa bekerja tetapi berupa kode kustom yang harus dirawat. Alarm CPU mengukur beban, bukan event cluster. Audit logging mencatat koneksi dan query, bukan event maintenance. Catatan: event Redshift juga tersedia di EventBridge, tetapi soal ini meminta fitur bawaan Redshift. Aturan: event cluster Redshift → event subscription ke SNS.","r":["Salah — CPU utilization tidak mengindikasikan maintenance, penggantian node, atau snapshot gagal.","Salah — Polling dengan Lambda adalah kode kustom yang melanggar persyaratan.","Benar — Event subscription Redshift mengirim notifikasi kategori event yang dipilih langsung ke SNS.","Salah — Audit logging mencatat aktivitas pengguna dan query, bukan event operasional cluster."],"k":"Tips ujian: Redshift/DMS/RDS 'event subscription' → notifikasi via SNS."},{"id":"E2A-31","d":2,"ts":"2.1.3","t":"DynamoDB to OpenSearch zero-ETL","q":"A company stores its product catalog in Amazon DynamoDB. The company now needs fuzzy, full-text search across product names and descriptions, with results reflecting catalog changes within seconds. The team wants to avoid writing and maintaining custom code to copy data between services. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Use the DynamoDB zero-ETL integration with Amazon OpenSearch Service to replicate the table into an OpenSearch index, and run searches in OpenSearch.","Add a GSI on the product name attribute and use begins_with conditions in Query operations.","Export the table to Amazon S3 every hour and query it with Amazon Athena using LIKE predicates.","Enable DynamoDB Streams and write an AWS Lambda function that indexes each change into an Amazon OpenSearch Service domain."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'fuzzy, full-text search', perubahan terlihat 'within seconds', dan 'avoid writing and maintaining custom code'. Integrasi zero-ETL DynamoDB dengan Amazon OpenSearch Service (berbasis OpenSearch Ingestion) mereplikasi data tabel ke index OpenSearch secara near-real-time tanpa kode kustom, lalu OpenSearch menyediakan pencarian teks penuh dan fuzzy matching. Distraktor terdekat adalah DynamoDB Streams + Lambda: hasilnya sama, tetapi tim harus menulis dan memelihara kode pengindeksan, penanganan error, dan retry. GSI dengan begins_with hanya mendukung pencocokan prefix, bukan pencarian fuzzy di dalam teks. Ekspor per jam ke S3 dan Athena tidak memenuhi latensi detik. Aturan umum: data operasional di DynamoDB + kebutuhan search → zero-ETL ke OpenSearch; tanpa kode kustom lebih disukai.","r":["Benar — Integrasi zero-ETL menyalin perubahan DynamoDB ke OpenSearch secara near-real-time tanpa kode kustom, dan OpenSearch menyediakan full-text search.","Salah — begins_with pada GSI hanya mencocokkan awalan; tidak ada fuzzy atau pencarian kata di dalam deskripsi.","Salah — Ekspor per jam tidak memenuhi kebutuhan perubahan dalam hitungan detik, dan LIKE bukan pencarian fuzzy.","Salah — Berfungsi, tetapi memerlukan kode Lambda kustom yang harus dipelihara sehingga overhead lebih tinggi."],"k":"DynamoDB + full-text search, no custom code → DynamoDB zero-ETL integration with OpenSearch Service."},{"id":"E4B-08","d":4,"ts":"4.3.2","t":"Glue security configuration","q":"A compliance policy requires that all data produced by AWS Glue ETL jobs be encrypted with a customer managed AWS KMS key. This includes the output written to Amazon S3, the job logs written to Amazon CloudWatch Logs, and the job bookmark data. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST effort?","o":["Create an AWS Glue security configuration that enables S3 encryption with SSE-KMS, CloudWatch Logs encryption, and job bookmark encryption using the customer managed key, and attach it to the Glue jobs.","Enable default encryption with SSE-KMS on the output S3 bucket.","Enable encryption of the AWS Glue Data Catalog metadata using the customer managed key in the Data Catalog settings.","Add the Glue job role as a key user in the KMS key policy."],"a":[0],"e":"Syaratnya mencakup tiga hal sekaligus: output di S3, 'job logs written to CloudWatch Logs', dan 'job bookmark data', semuanya dengan customer managed key. AWS Glue security configuration adalah satu objek yang mengatur ketiganya: S3 encryption (SSE-KMS), CloudWatch Logs encryption, dan job bookmark encryption, lalu cukup di-attach ke job. Distraktor terdekat adalah default encryption pada bucket S3: hanya menutup output S3, sementara log dan bookmark tidak tercakup. Enkripsi Data Catalog hanya melindungi metadata katalog (dan password koneksi), bukan data job. Menambah role ke key policy diperlukan agar role bisa memakai kunci, tetapi tidak dengan sendirinya mengaktifkan enkripsi apa pun. Aturan umum: enkripsi output/log/bookmark Glue job → Glue security configuration; enkripsi metadata → Data Catalog encryption settings.","r":["Benar — Security configuration Glue mengenkripsi output S3, CloudWatch Logs, dan job bookmark dengan KMS key dalam satu konfigurasi.","Salah — Default encryption bucket hanya mencakup output S3, tidak mencakup log dan job bookmark.","Salah — Data Catalog encryption hanya melindungi metadata katalog, bukan data keluaran job.","Salah — Izin pada key policy diperlukan tetapi tidak mengaktifkan enkripsi pada output, log, atau bookmark."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'encrypt Glue job output + CloudWatch logs + job bookmarks' → Glue security configuration."},{"id":"E4A-44","d":4,"ts":"4.2.4","t":"Lake Formation LF-Tag based access control","q":"A data lake governed by AWS Lake Formation contains 600 tables, and data engineers add about 20 new tables each week. Each table and some columns are classified as confidentiality=public, internal, or restricted. Analysts must automatically get SELECT access to all public and internal data, including new tables, without data stewards granting access table by table. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Grant analysts SELECT on each table by using named resource grants, and add grants as new tables are created.","Create an IAM policy with s3:GetObject on the S3 prefixes of public and internal tables.","Define an LF-Tag confidentiality with the values public, internal, and restricted, assign the tags to databases, tables, and columns, and grant analysts SELECT on the tag expression confidentiality IN (public, internal).","Create a separate Glue Data Catalog database for each confidentiality level and copy the tables into the matching database."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: '600 tables', 'about 20 new tables each week', dan 'without ... table by table'. Lake Formation tag-based access control (LF-TBAC) memberi izin berdasarkan ekspresi LF-Tag, bukan berdasarkan nama resource. Begitu tabel atau kolom baru diberi tag yang sesuai (atau mewarisi tag dari database), analis otomatis mendapat akses tanpa grant baru. Tag di level kolom memungkinkan kolom restricted dikecualikan walaupun tabelnya internal. Named resource grant menuntut grant per tabel dan tidak skalabel. Akses langsung S3 lewat IAM melewati kontrol Lake Formation dan tidak mendukung pembatasan kolom. Menyalin tabel menggandakan data dan pipeline. Aturan umum: banyak resource yang terus bertambah → LF-Tags; sedikit resource yang stabil → named resource grants.","r":["Salah — Grant per tabel tidak skalabel untuk ratusan tabel yang terus bertambah.","Salah — Akses S3 langsung melewati Lake Formation dan tidak mendukung kontrol per kolom.","Benar — LF-TBAC memberi akses otomatis ke resource yang ditag, termasuk tabel baru dan kolom tertentu.","Salah — Duplikasi data dan pipeline menambah biaya serta overhead."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'hundreds of tables, new tables added, grant by classification' → Lake Formation LF-Tags (LF-TBAC)."},{"id":"E2A-20","d":2,"ts":"2.1.2","t":"EMR node types and scaling","q":"A company runs Apache Spark jobs on an Amazon EMR cluster that stores input and output data in Amazon S3. During month-end, the jobs need about 3 times more compute capacity for a few hours. The company wants to add capacity cheaply without risking loss of any HDFS data if instances are reclaimed. Which configuration should a data engineer use?","o":["Add core nodes that use Spot Instances.","Change the primary node to a larger instance type.","Add task nodes that use Spot Instances, and enable EMR managed scaling.","Add core nodes that use On-Demand Instances and keep them permanently."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci adalah kebutuhan compute sementara 'for a few hours', 'cheaply', dan 'without risking loss of any HDFS data'. Task node pada EMR hanya menjalankan task dan tidak menyimpan blok HDFS, sehingga jika Spot Instance diambil kembali, tidak ada data HDFS yang hilang; job hanya mengulang task yang terputus. EMR managed scaling menambah dan mengurangi node otomatis sesuai beban, sehingga kapasitas tambahan hilang setelah lonjakan selesai. Distraktor terdekat adalah core node Spot: murah, tetapi core node menyimpan HDFS sehingga interupsi dapat menyebabkan kehilangan data atau kegagalan job. Core node On-Demand permanen membayar kapasitas idle sepanjang bulan. Primary node lebih besar tidak menambah kapasitas pemrosesan. Aturan umum: kapasitas burst murah di EMR → task node Spot + managed scaling; core node menyimpan HDFS.","r":["Salah — Core node menyimpan blok HDFS; Spot interruption dapat menyebabkan kehilangan data atau job gagal.","Salah — Primary node mengoordinasikan cluster dan tidak menambah kapasitas pemrosesan task.","Benar — Task node tidak menyimpan HDFS, sehingga Spot aman dan murah, dan managed scaling menyesuaikan kapasitas otomatis.","Salah — Menambah core node permanen membayar kapasitas yang hanya diperlukan beberapa jam per bulan."],"k":"EMR burst capacity murah → Spot task nodes (tanpa HDFS) + managed scaling."},{"id":"E4B-04","d":4,"ts":"4.3.1","t":"CloudWatch Logs data protection","q":"A data pipeline application sends logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. An audit found that some log events contain credit card numbers and email addresses. Compliance requires that this data is masked for everyone who reads the logs, except members of the security team who must be able to view the original values when investigating incidents. Which TWO actions should a data engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Create a CloudWatch Logs data protection policy on the log group that uses managed data identifiers for credit card numbers and email addresses.","Associate a customer managed AWS KMS key with the log group so the log events are encrypted at rest.","Create a subscription filter that sends log events to an AWS Lambda function that removes sensitive values and writes them to a new log group.","Grant the logs:Unmask permission only to the IAM role that the security team uses.","Enable Amazon Macie on the log group to classify and mask the sensitive data."],"a":[0,3],"e":"Kebutuhan kuncinya adalah data 'masked for everyone ... except members of the security team' yang tetap bisa melihat nilai asli. CloudWatch Logs data protection policy memakai managed data identifiers (misalnya CreditCardNumber, EmailAddress) untuk mendeteksi dan memasking data sensitif pada log group saat ditampilkan. Pengguna yang memiliki izin IAM logs:Unmask dapat melihat nilai asli, sehingga cukup berikan izin itu hanya ke role tim security. Distraktor terdekat adalah subscription filter + Lambda: log asli tetap tersimpan tanpa masking di log group sumber, dan Anda harus memelihara kode kustom. Enkripsi KMS pada log group melindungi data at rest, tetapi siapa pun yang punya akses baca tetap melihat plaintext. Macie hanya memindai Amazon S3, bukan CloudWatch Logs. Perlu diingat: masking hanya berlaku untuk log event yang di-ingest setelah policy dibuat; event lama tidak ikut ter-masking. Aturan umum: masking PII di CloudWatch Logs → data protection policy + logs:Unmask untuk pihak yang berwenang.","r":["Benar — Data protection policy mendeteksi dan memasking kartu kredit dan email di log group secara otomatis.","Salah — KMS hanya mengenkripsi at rest; pembaca dengan izin tetap melihat nilai asli tanpa masking.","Salah — Log asli tetap tidak ter-masking di log group sumber dan solusi ini menambah kode yang harus dirawat.","Benar — logs:Unmask memungkinkan hanya tim security melihat nilai asli yang ter-masking.","Salah — Macie tidak memindai CloudWatch Logs; Macie bekerja pada objek Amazon S3."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'mask sensitive data in CloudWatch Logs, only some users can see it' → data protection policy + logs:Unmask."},{"id":"E3A-32","d":3,"ts":"3.1.8","t":"Lambda limits and alternatives","q":"A data engineer currently uses an AWS Lambda function triggered by Amazon S3 uploads to decompress and re-partition large archive files. As file sizes have grown, processing now takes 35 to 60 minutes per file, and invocations fail with timeouts. The engineer wants to keep the solution event-driven and serverless with minimal code changes to the existing Python container image. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Increase the Lambda function timeout to 60 minutes.","Increase the Lambda function memory to 10,240 MB so that it always finishes within 15 minutes.","Use an Amazon EventBridge rule for the S3 Object Created event that runs the existing container image as an Amazon ECS task on AWS Fargate.","Split the work across a chain of Lambda functions that each process part of the file and pass state in environment variables."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'takes 35 to 60 minutes', 'fail with timeouts', 'event-driven and serverless', dan 'existing Python container image'. Lambda punya batas waktu maksimum 15 menit yang tidak bisa dinaikkan, sehingga pekerjaan 35 sampai 60 menit tidak cocok lagi untuk Lambda. EventBridge dapat menerima event S3 Object Created dan langsung menjalankan ECS task di AWS Fargate yang memakai container image yang sudah ada, tetap serverless tanpa server untuk dikelola dan tanpa batas 15 menit. Menaikkan timeout ke 60 menit tidak mungkin. Menaikkan memori mempercepat sebagian proses, tetapi tidak menjamin pekerjaan 60 menit selesai dalam 15 menit. Merantai Lambda dengan state di environment variable rapuh dan tidak dirancang untuk itu. Aturan umum: pekerjaan lebih dari 15 menit → Fargate, Glue, Batch, atau EMR, bukan Lambda.","r":["Salah — Timeout Lambda maksimum 15 menit dan tidak bisa dinaikkan.","Salah — Memori lebih besar tidak menjamin pekerjaan 60 menit selesai dalam 15 menit.","Benar — EventBridge memicu task Fargate dengan image yang sama, serverless, dan tanpa batas 15 menit.","Salah — Rantai Lambda dengan state di environment variable rapuh dan rumit."],"k":"Tips ujian: proses lebih dari 15 menit → bukan Lambda; pakai Fargate/Glue/Batch yang dipicu EventBridge atau Step Functions."},{"id":"E3B-66","d":3,"ts":"3.4.5","t":"Broadcast join to avoid skew","q":"An AWS Glue job joins a 4 TB sales fact dataset with a 40 MB product dimension dataset on product_id. A few popular products account for most of the sales rows, and the shuffle join stage shows severe task skew. Which solution will MOST effectively eliminate the skewed shuffle?","o":["Increase the number of workers in the Glue job.","Sort the fact dataset by product_id before the join.","Convert the dimension dataset to CSV format.","Use a broadcast join so that the small product dataset is sent to every executor and the fact data is joined without being shuffled by product_id."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kuncinya: satu sisi join sangat kecil ('40 MB'), sisi lain besar ('4 TB') dan 'severe task skew' pada shuffle join. Broadcast join mengirim salinan dataset kecil ke setiap executor sehingga dataset besar tidak perlu di-shuffle berdasarkan product_id; tanpa shuffle, kunci populer tidak lagi menumpuk di satu task. Distraktor terdekat adalah menambah worker: shuffle tetap mengirim semua baris produk populer ke satu partisi sehingga task panas tetap lambat. Sorting juga memerlukan shuffle dan tidak menghilangkan skew. Format CSV tidak relevan. Aturan: join tabel besar dengan tabel kecil + skew → broadcast join; jika kedua sisi besar → salting atau AQE skew join.","r":["Salah — Worker tambahan tidak memecah partisi shuffle yang berisi kunci populer.","Salah — Sorting membutuhkan shuffle dan tidak menghilangkan konsentrasi kunci populer.","Salah — Format file dimensi tidak memengaruhi skew pada join.","Benar — Broadcast join menghindari shuffle dataset besar sehingga skew pada product_id tidak lagi terjadi."],"k":"Tips ujian: big table JOIN small table (MB) dengan skew → broadcast join."},{"id":"E3B-56","d":3,"ts":"3.4.3","t":"Resolving inconsistent duplicates with DataBrew","q":"A customer table in Amazon S3 contains duplicate records that differ only in letter casing and leading or trailing spaces in the name and email columns (for example, ' Ana@Example.com' and 'ana@example.com'). Business analysts want to investigate and fix these inconsistencies without code as part of a recurring preparation job. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST effort?","o":["Train an AWS Glue FindMatches ML transform with labeled examples to find fuzzy duplicates.","Use an AWS Glue DataBrew recipe that trims whitespace, converts the columns to lowercase, and then removes duplicate rows, and run it as a scheduled recipe job.","Load the data into Amazon Redshift and declare email as a PRIMARY KEY.","Use Amazon Macie to detect the duplicate email addresses."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya: duplikat yang 'differ only in letter casing and spaces' (masalah deterministik), 'without code', dan 'recurring'. DataBrew recipe dapat menormalisasi data dengan langkah trim dan lowercase lalu menghapus duplicate rows, kemudian dijalankan sebagai recipe job terjadwal. Distraktor terdekat adalah FindMatches: cocok untuk pencocokan fuzzy tanpa kunci (salah ketik, ejaan berbeda), tetapi butuh pelabelan dan pelatihan — berlebihan untuk masalah yang dapat diselesaikan dengan normalisasi sederhana. PRIMARY KEY di Redshift bersifat informasional dan tidak ditegakkan. Macie mendeteksi data sensitif, bukan duplikat. Aturan: inkonsistensi format sederhana → normalisasi dengan DataBrew; fuzzy match tanpa kunci → FindMatches.","r":["Salah — FindMatches membutuhkan pelabelan dan pelatihan, berlebihan untuk masalah casing dan spasi.","Benar — Recipe trim, lowercase, dan remove duplicates menyelesaikan inkonsistensi tanpa kode dan bisa dijadwalkan.","Salah — Redshift tidak menegakkan PRIMARY KEY, sehingga duplikat tetap masuk.","Salah — Macie mengidentifikasi data sensitif, bukan menghapus duplikat."],"k":"Tips ujian: duplikat karena casing/spasi → normalisasi + remove duplicates (DataBrew); fuzzy tanpa kunci → FindMatches."},{"id":"E3B-45","d":3,"ts":"3.4.1","t":"DQDL DataFreshness","q":"A Glue job publishes a curated inventory table that downstream systems assume is updated at least once a day. An upstream extract sometimes silently stops delivering new records, and the job still succeeds with stale data. The team wants the data quality ruleset to fail when the newest last_updated timestamp in the dataset is older than 24 hours. Which DQDL rule should the team add?","o":["DataFreshness \"last_updated\" <= 24 hours","IsComplete \"last_updated\"","RowCount > 0","IsUnique \"last_updated\""],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'silently stops delivering new records' dan 'older than 24 hours'. Rule DataFreshness di DQDL memeriksa selisih waktu antara nilai timestamp pada kolom dan waktu evaluasi, sehingga data yang basi dapat terdeteksi meskipun job sukses. Distraktor terdekat adalah RowCount > 0: dataset basi tetap memiliki baris (data lama), sehingga rule lolos dan masalah tidak tertangkap. IsComplete hanya memastikan kolom tidak kosong, dan IsUnique memeriksa duplikat. Aturan: 'data must be no older than X' → DataFreshness.","r":["Benar — DataFreshness menggagalkan evaluasi bila timestamp terbaru lebih tua dari 24 jam.","Salah — Kolom bisa terisi lengkap tetapi tetap berisi data basi.","Salah — Data basi tetap memiliki baris sehingga rule tetap lolos.","Salah — Keunikan timestamp tidak menunjukkan kesegaran data."],"k":"Tips ujian: stale data / 'updated within X hours' → DQDL DataFreshness."},{"id":"E1B-20","d":1,"ts":"1.2.2","t":"Secrets Manager for Glue connections","q":"A data engineer is configuring several AWS Glue JDBC connections to Amazon RDS databases. Security policy prohibits storing database passwords in job scripts or job parameters, and the passwords must be rotated automatically every 30 days. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Store the credentials in AWS Secrets Manager with automatic rotation enabled, reference the secret in the Glue connection, and grant the Glue job role permission to read the secret.","Store the credentials as Glue job parameters and update them with a scheduled AWS Lambda function every 30 days.","Store the credentials in a text file in Amazon S3 encrypted with SSE-S3 and read the file at the start of each job.","Store the credentials as String parameters in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store and update them manually every 30 days."],"a":[0],"e":"Persyaratan penentunya adalah larangan menyimpan password di skrip atau parameter job, serta 'rotated automatically every 30 days' dengan 'LEAST operational overhead'. AWS Secrets Manager menyediakan rotasi otomatis bawaan untuk kredensial database RDS, dan Glue connection dapat mereferensikan secret secara langsung sehingga job tidak pernah menyimpan password. Peran IAM job hanya membutuhkan izin untuk membaca secret tersebut. Parameter Store String adalah distraktor terdekat, tetapi tidak terenkripsi sebagai SecureString dan tidak memiliki rotasi otomatis sehingga pembaruan manual menambah beban. Menyimpan di job parameters melanggar kebijakan, dan file teks di S3 adalah praktik yang lemah serta tanpa rotasi. Aturan umum: kredensial database + rotasi otomatis → AWS Secrets Manager.","r":["Benar — Secrets Manager menyediakan rotasi otomatis dan diintegrasikan langsung dengan Glue connection.","Salah — Melanggar larangan menyimpan password di job parameters dan membutuhkan logika rotasi kustom.","Salah — File kredensial di S3 bukan praktik aman dan tidak menyediakan rotasi otomatis.","Salah — Parameter String tidak dienkripsi dan tidak ada rotasi otomatis; pembaruan manual menambah overhead."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'automatic rotation of DB credentials' → AWS Secrets Manager (bukan Parameter Store)."},{"id":"E4A-33","d":4,"ts":"4.2.1","t":"Explicit deny with principal exception","q":"An Amazon S3 bucket stores audit extracts. Several administrators have the AdministratorAccess managed policy. Company policy states that nobody may delete objects in the bucket except a dedicated break-glass IAM role, and this rule must apply even to administrators. Which solution meets this requirement?","o":["Add a bucket policy statement that denies s3:DeleteObject and s3:DeleteObjectVersion for all principals when aws:PrincipalArn does not equal the ARN of the break-glass role.","Remove AdministratorAccess from all administrators and grant them read-only access.","Enable S3 Object Lock in compliance mode with a 10-year retention period.","Create a custom IAM policy for the break-glass role that allows s3:DeleteObject on the bucket."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'nobody may delete ... except a dedicated break-glass role' dan 'even to administrators'. Dalam evaluasi policy AWS, explicit deny selalu mengalahkan allow, termasuk allow dari AdministratorAccess. Custom bucket policy dengan Deny untuk aksi hapus dan kondisi ArnNotEquals/StringNotEquals pada aws:PrincipalArn memblokir semua principal kecuali role break-glass. Mencabut AdministratorAccess berdampak pada pekerjaan admin lainnya dan tidak mencegah pemberian izin hapus di masa depan. Object Lock compliance mode mencegah penghapusan oleh siapa pun, termasuk role break-glass, sehingga melanggar pengecualian. Memberi allow ke role break-glass saja tidak mencegah admin menghapus. Aturan umum: 'semua kecuali satu principal' → explicit Deny dengan kondisi aws:PrincipalArn.","r":["Benar — Explicit deny dengan pengecualian aws:PrincipalArn berlaku bahkan untuk administrator dan tetap mengizinkan role break-glass.","Salah — Mengganggu tugas admin lain dan tidak menjamin aturan tetap berlaku jika izin diberikan lagi.","Salah — Compliance mode mencegah penghapusan oleh siapa pun, termasuk role break-glass.","Salah — Allow untuk role break-glass tidak mencegah admin yang sudah punya izin penuh."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'deny everyone except X, even admins' → explicit Deny + kondisi aws:PrincipalArn (ArnNotEquals)."},{"id":"E1A-66","d":1,"ts":"1.1.11","t":"AWS Glue job bookmark reset","q":"An AWS Glue ETL job with job bookmarks enabled processes new files from an Amazon S3 prefix every night. A bug in the transformation logic was fixed, and the team must reprocess all files in the prefix with the corrected logic. Which action should the data engineer take with the LEAST effort?","o":["Reset the job bookmark for the job and run it again.","Copy all the files to a new prefix and create a new job.","Disable S3 Versioning on the bucket and rerun the job.","Delete and recreate the AWS Glue Data Catalog table."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: job memakai 'job bookmarks' dan tim harus 'reprocess all files' dengan 'LEAST effort'. Job bookmarks menyimpan state file yang sudah diproses sehingga run berikutnya melewatinya; karena itu menjalankan ulang job saja tidak akan memproses file lama. Mereset bookmark (misalnya dengan reset-job-bookmark) menghapus state tersebut sehingga run berikutnya memproses seluruh file lagi. Pastikan output ditulis ulang secara idempotent (misalnya overwrite partisi) agar tidak terjadi duplikasi. Distraktor terdekat adalah menyalin file ke prefix baru dan membuat job baru: berfungsi, tetapi effort dan biaya penyimpanan lebih besar. Versioning dan tabel katalog tidak memengaruhi state bookmark. Aturan umum: reprocess data di Glue dengan bookmarks = reset (atau rewind) job bookmark.","r":["Benar — Reset job bookmark menghapus state sehingga semua file diproses ulang dengan effort minimal.","Salah — Berfungsi tetapi butuh menyalin data dan membuat job baru, effort lebih besar.","Salah — Versioning tidak memengaruhi state job bookmark.","Salah — Membuat ulang tabel katalog tidak menghapus state bookmark job."],"k":"Glue reprocess semua data → reset job bookmark (output idempotent)."},{"id":"E3A-42","d":3,"ts":"3.2.1","t":"Managed Grafana vs Quick Sight","q":"A platform team needs near-real-time dashboards of operational metrics such as pipeline throughput, consumer lag, and error rates. The data comes from Amazon CloudWatch and a Prometheus-compatible metrics store, and the engineers want alerting and the open-source Grafana dashboard experience they already know. Separately, the business team needs governed sales dashboards. Which service should the data engineer use for the operational dashboards?","o":["Amazon Quick Sight with SPICE datasets refreshed every hour.","Amazon Managed Grafana with CloudWatch and Prometheus data sources.","AWS Glue DataBrew data profile dashboards.","Amazon Athena notebooks with matplotlib charts."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'near-real-time operational metrics', 'CloudWatch and Prometheus', 'alerting', dan 'Grafana experience they already know'. Amazon Managed Grafana adalah layanan Grafana terkelola dengan data source bawaan untuk CloudWatch, Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus, dan lainnya, cocok untuk dashboard observabilitas dan alerting. Quick Sight adalah alat BI untuk analitik bisnis, jadi tepat untuk dashboard penjualan, tetapi SPICE yang di-refresh per jam tidak memenuhi kebutuhan near-real-time metrik operasional. Profile DataBrew untuk memahami isi dataset, bukan memantau metrik. Notebook Athena untuk eksplorasi ad hoc, bukan dashboard operasional yang terus berjalan. Aturan umum: metrik operasional/observabilitas → Managed Grafana; dashboard bisnis/BI → Quick Sight.","r":["Salah — Refresh per jam tidak near-real-time, dan Quick Sight ditujukan untuk BI bisnis.","Benar — Managed Grafana mendukung CloudWatch dan Prometheus, near-real-time, dengan alerting yang familier bagi tim.","Salah — Profile DataBrew menganalisis isi dataset, bukan memantau metrik operasional.","Salah — Notebook cocok untuk eksplorasi ad hoc, bukan dashboard operasional yang selalu aktif."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'operational metrics / Prometheus / Grafana' → Amazon Managed Grafana; 'business BI dashboards' → Quick Sight."},{"id":"E1A-08","d":1,"ts":"1.1.1","t":"Data Firehose with MSK source","q":"A company uses an Amazon MSK provisioned cluster with IAM access control. A new requirement asks for all messages from one topic to be archived in Amazon S3 with the LEAST operational overhead and without writing consumer code. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Deploy a Kafka consumer application on Amazon EC2 that writes batches of messages to Amazon S3.","Use AWS DMS with the MSK cluster as a source endpoint and Amazon S3 as the target endpoint.","Create an Amazon Data Firehose stream with the MSK cluster topic as the source and Amazon S3 as the destination.","Configure Amazon S3 Event Notifications on the destination bucket to pull messages from MSK."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'LEAST operational overhead' dan 'without writing consumer code'. Amazon Data Firehose mendukung MSK sebagai sumber: Firehose membaca topik MSK lalu mengirim data ke S3 dengan buffering, kompresi, dan retry yang dikelola AWS. Distraktor terdekat adalah consumer di EC2: memang bekerja, tetapi berarti menulis dan mengoperasikan kode consumer serta server. DMS mendukung Kafka/MSK sebagai target, bukan sebagai sumber, sehingga opsi tersebut tidak valid. S3 Event Notifications hanya memancarkan event saat objek berubah di bucket, tidak bisa menarik data dari Kafka. Aturan umum: arsip topik MSK atau stream KDS ke S3 tanpa kode = Firehose dengan sumber MSK/KDS.","r":["Salah — Memerlukan kode consumer dan pengelolaan EC2, bertentangan dengan least overhead.","Salah — Di DMS, Kafka/MSK adalah target endpoint, bukan sumber.","Benar — Firehose mendukung MSK sebagai sumber dan mengirim ke S3 secara fully managed.","Salah — S3 Event Notifications tidak dapat membaca data dari MSK; fitur ini hanya memberi tahu perubahan objek di bucket."],"k":"MSK/KDS → S3 tanpa kode → Data Firehose (source = MSK atau KDS)."},{"id":"E2B-44","d":2,"ts":"2.3.3","t":"Object Lock retention with Lifecycle expiration","q":"A regulation requires that trade confirmation files in Amazon S3 be kept unchanged for exactly 1 year so that no user, including administrators, can delete or overwrite them during that time. After 1 year, the files must be deleted automatically. Which TWO actions should the data engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Enable S3 Object Lock on the bucket and set a default retention of 365 days in compliance mode.","Enable S3 Object Lock with a default retention of 365 days in governance mode.","Create an S3 Lifecycle rule that expires objects after 366 days and permanently deletes their noncurrent versions.","Use an IAM policy that denies s3:DeleteObject for all users for 1 year.","Enable MFA Delete and give the MFA device to the security team."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'no user, including administrators, can delete or overwrite' selama 1 tahun, lalu 'deleted automatically'. S3 Object Lock compliance mode membuat versi objek WORM: tidak ada pengguna, termasuk root, yang bisa menghapus atau mengubah retensi sebelum periode berakhir. Object Lock otomatis mengaktifkan versioning. Setelah retensi habis, Lifecycle rule dengan Expiration dan NoncurrentVersionExpiration menghapus data secara otomatis; karena bucket berversi, versi noncurrent juga harus dihapus agar data benar-benar hilang. Governance mode bisa dilewati oleh pengguna dengan izin s3:BypassGovernanceRetention, jadi tidak memenuhi syarat administrator. IAM deny bisa diubah oleh administrator. MFA Delete hanya menambah langkah, bukan WORM. Ingat: WORM wajib untuk semua termasuk root → Object Lock compliance mode; hapus otomatis setelahnya → Lifecycle expiration.","r":["Benar — Compliance mode mencegah siapa pun, termasuk root, menghapus atau menimpa versi objek selama 365 hari.","Salah — Governance mode bisa dilewati oleh pengguna dengan izin bypass, sehingga administrator tetap bisa menghapus.","Benar — Lifecycle expiration plus penghapusan versi noncurrent menghapus data otomatis setelah retensi berakhir.","Salah — IAM policy bisa diubah oleh administrator, sehingga bukan perlindungan WORM.","Salah — MFA Delete hanya menambah autentikasi; pemegang MFA tetap bisa menghapus."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'even root cannot delete' → Object Lock compliance mode; governance mode = bisa di-bypass."},{"id":"E2C-42","d":2,"ts":"2.4.6","t":"Bedrock knowledge base hierarchical chunking","q":"A company is building an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base over long equipment maintenance manuals. Each manual has chapters and sections. Testing shows that small chunks give precise matches but the model's answers lack surrounding context, while large chunks reduce retrieval precision. Which chunking strategy should the data engineer configure?","o":["Fixed-size chunking with a larger maximum token size.","No chunking, so each manual is a single chunk.","Hierarchical chunking with smaller child chunks for retrieval and larger parent chunks returned as context.","Default chunking of about 300 tokens."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah trade-off antara chunk kecil yang presisi dan kebutuhan konteks yang lebih luas. Hierarchical chunking di Amazon Bedrock knowledge base membuat struktur parent dan child chunk; pencarian dilakukan pada child chunk yang kecil sehingga embedding lebih presisi, lalu child chunk diganti dengan parent chunk yang lebih besar saat dikembalikan ke model agar konteks lengkap. Fixed-size dengan ukuran lebih besar mengembalikan masalah turunnya presisi retrieval. Tanpa chunking, seluruh manual menjadi satu vektor sehingga retrieval sangat tidak presisi dan bisa melampaui batas token. Default chunking sekitar 300 token sama dengan kondisi chunk kecil yang kurang konteks. Aturan umum: butuh presisi sekaligus konteks luas pada dokumen terstruktur → hierarchical chunking.","r":["Salah — Chunk lebih besar menurunkan presisi retrieval, yang merupakan masalah yang ingin dihindari.","Salah — Satu chunk per manual membuat embedding terlalu umum dan retrieval tidak presisi.","Benar — Child chunk kecil untuk presisi pencarian, parent chunk besar untuk konteks jawaban.","Salah — Default sekitar 300 token tetap kecil sehingga konteks tetap kurang."],"k":"Tips ujian: presisi retrieval + konteks luas → hierarchical chunking (child untuk cari, parent untuk konteks)."},{"id":"E2C-32","d":2,"ts":"2.4.5","t":"Partitioning vs bucketing","q":"A data engineer is designing the S3 layout for an Athena table of 5 billion purchase events per year. Queries filter by purchase date and, frequently, by customer_id (about 20 million distinct customers). A colleague proposes partitioning by date and customer_id. Which design should the data engineer choose to optimize query performance?","o":["Partition by customer_id only so that each customer has its own prefix.","Partition by date and customer_id as proposed.","Do not partition the data and rely on Parquet statistics only.","Partition by date and bucket the data by customer_id within each partition."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah customer_id dengan sekitar 20 juta nilai berbeda (kardinalitas sangat tinggi) yang juga sering difilter. Partisi berdasarkan kolom berkardinalitas tinggi menghasilkan jutaan partisi dan file sangat kecil, sehingga metadata partisi membengkak dan query melambat. Pola yang direkomendasikan adalah partisi berdasarkan kolom berkardinalitas rendah yang selalu difilter (tanggal) dan bucketing pada kolom berkardinalitas tinggi (customer_id), yang mengelompokkan data ke sejumlah file tetap per partisi sehingga Athena hanya membaca bucket yang relevan. Partisi hanya pada customer_id kehilangan pruning tanggal dan tetap menimbulkan jutaan partisi. Tanpa partisi, setiap query memindai seluruh data walaupun statistik Parquet sedikit membantu. Aturan umum: kardinalitas rendah → partition; kardinalitas tinggi → bucket.","r":["Salah — Jutaan partisi customer_id menciptakan file kecil dan overhead metadata besar, serta tidak ada pruning tanggal.","Salah — Kombinasi tanggal dan customer_id menghasilkan miliaran kombinasi partisi dan masalah small files.","Salah — Tanpa partisi, filter tanggal tidak bisa memangkas prefix sehingga data yang dipindai besar.","Benar — Partisi tanggal untuk pruning dan bucketing customer_id untuk membatasi file yang dibaca tanpa ledakan partisi."],"k":"Tips ujian: kolom berkardinalitas tinggi → bucketing, bukan partitioning."},{"id":"E1C-08","d":1,"ts":"1.3.1","t":"Step Functions callback pattern","q":"Before a monthly financial dataset is loaded into the production Amazon Redshift cluster, a data steward must review a summary and approve the load. Approval can take up to 3 days. The rest of the pipeline is already automated with AWS Glue and AWS Lambda. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Use an AWS Step Functions Express workflow with a Wait state that pauses for 3 days.","Use an AWS Step Functions Standard workflow with a task that uses the .waitForTaskToken callback pattern to send the task token to the approver through Amazon SNS, and resume the workflow when the approval action calls SendTaskSuccess.","Use an Amazon SQS delay queue set to 3 days before the Redshift load Lambda function processes the message.","Have the Lambda function that sends the approval email wait in a loop until the approver updates an Amazon DynamoDB item."],"a":[1],"e":"Kebutuhan kuncinya adalah langkah 'approve' oleh manusia yang bisa memakan 'up to 3 days'. Step Functions Standard workflow dapat berjalan hingga 1 tahun, dan pola callback '.waitForTaskToken' menghentikan eksekusi sampai sistem eksternal (misalnya link approval via API Gateway/Lambda) memanggil SendTaskSuccess atau SendTaskFailure dengan token tersebut. Distractor terdekat adalah Express workflow: durasi maksimumnya hanya 5 menit sehingga tidak bisa menunggu 3 hari. Delay queue SQS maksimum 15 menit dan tidak menangkap keputusan approve/reject. Lambda yang menunggu dalam loop dibatasi timeout 15 menit. Aturan umum: human approval atau menunggu sistem eksternal lama → Standard workflow + task token callback.","r":["Salah — Express workflow dibatasi maksimum 5 menit dan Wait tetap tidak menangkap keputusan approver.","Benar — Standard workflow bisa menunggu lama, dan callback task token melanjutkan eksekusi hanya setelah approver merespons.","Salah — Delay queue SQS maksimal 15 menit dan tidak membawa hasil approve atau reject.","Salah — Lambda dibatasi 15 menit, sehingga tidak bisa menunggu hingga 3 hari."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'manual approval' / 'wait for external system' → Step Functions Standard + .waitForTaskToken."},{"id":"E1C-21","d":1,"ts":"1.3.2","t":"Highly available serverless orchestration","q":"A company runs its entire nightly ETL orchestration from a cron script on a single Amazon EC2 instance. Last month the instance had a hardware failure and no pipelines ran for two days before anyone noticed. The company wants a highly available orchestration layer with the LEAST operational overhead. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create an Auto Scaling group with two EC2 instances in different Availability Zones, both running the same cron script.","Move the cron script to a larger EC2 instance type with enhanced networking.","Replace the cron script with an Amazon EventBridge Scheduler schedule that starts an AWS Step Functions state machine, and alert on failed executions through Amazon CloudWatch alarms and Amazon SNS.","Run the cron script in a Docker container on a single EC2 instance with a restart policy."],"a":[2],"e":"Kebutuhannya 'highly available orchestration' dengan 'LEAST operational overhead' setelah kegagalan single instance. EventBridge Scheduler dan Step Functions adalah layanan regional terkelola yang secara bawaan berjalan di beberapa Availability Zone, jadi tidak ada server yang bisa mati atau perlu dipatch. Menambahkan alarm CloudWatch pada metrik eksekusi gagal yang dikirim via SNS memastikan masalah segera diketahui. Distractor terdekat adalah Auto Scaling group dua instance: lebih tersedia, tetapi kedua instance menjalankan cron yang sama sehingga pipeline berjalan ganda, dan server tetap harus dikelola. Instance yang lebih besar atau container dengan restart policy tetap single point of failure di satu host. Aturan umum: ganti cron di EC2 dengan EventBridge Scheduler + Step Functions untuk ketersediaan tinggi tanpa server.","r":["Salah — Dua instance menjalankan cron yang sama menyebabkan eksekusi ganda dan tetap ada overhead server.","Salah — Instance lebih besar tetap single point of failure.","Benar — Layanan serverless multi-AZ menghilangkan single point of failure, dan alarm SNS memberi peringatan kegagalan.","Salah — Restart policy tidak membantu bila host EC2-nya sendiri gagal."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'cron on single EC2' + 'highly available' → EventBridge Scheduler + Step Functions/Lambda."},{"id":"E3B-04","d":3,"ts":"3.3.5","t":"CloudTrail organization trail and integrity validation","q":"A company has 40 AWS accounts in AWS Organizations. Auditors require that API activity from all current and future accounts is captured in a single location, and that the company can prove the log files were not modified or deleted after delivery. Which TWO actions should a data engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Create an organization trail in the management account that delivers to a central S3 bucket in a dedicated log archive account.","Enable CloudTrail log file integrity validation on the trail.","Create a separate trail in each member account that delivers to an S3 bucket in the same account.","Enable SSE-S3 default encryption on the log bucket as proof that the files were not modified.","Export the CloudTrail Event history from each account to CSV every month."],"a":[0,1],"e":"Ada dua persyaratan: 'all current and future accounts' di 'single location', dan 'prove the log files were not modified'. Organization trail yang dibuat di management account otomatis berlaku untuk semua akun anggota, termasuk akun baru, dan bisa dikirim ke bucket terpusat di akun log archive. Log file integrity validation membuat digest file bertanda tangan (SHA-256 + signing) sehingga perubahan atau penghapusan file bisa dibuktikan. Distraktor trail per akun tidak terpusat dan tidak otomatis mencakup akun baru. Enkripsi SSE-S3 melindungi kerahasiaan, bukan membuktikan integritas. Aturan: multi-account → organization trail; tamper-evident → log file integrity validation.","r":["Benar — Organization trail mencakup semua akun saat ini dan akun baru, dengan log terpusat di satu bucket.","Benar — Integrity validation menghasilkan digest file sehingga modifikasi atau penghapusan log bisa dideteksi dan dibuktikan.","Salah — Trail per akun tidak terpusat dan akun baru harus dikonfigurasi manual.","Salah — Enkripsi at rest tidak membuktikan bahwa isi file tidak diubah.","Salah — Event history hanya management events 90 hari dan ekspor manual tidak memberi bukti integritas."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'all accounts including new ones' → organization trail; 'prove not tampered' → log file integrity validation."}]});